@540[4]. (This) can be seen from common intuition.

@569[10]. The other limit is the seeing -intuitivum- and thinking [faculty].

@790[9]. All things which are in the natural mind from the spiritual mind come under the view, and into the perception, of the man.

@815[5]. Faith is acknowledgement, and a view from acknowledgement.

@1032[2]. The interiors of the mind are (then) kept by the Lord in a looking to Himself.

@1086[end]. A man who is in genuine truths from the sense of the letter... can disperse the whole diabolical crew... by a mere look and an effort of will.

@Inv 42. No one can speak to another there unless he looks directly at him.

Vigour.; Vigor.

@SE 3317. Still, the external senses remained in their vigour.

Vile.; Vilis.
Despise. Hold cheap.; Vilipendere.
Become worthless.; Vilescere.

@AC 950. They held the Lord as vile.

@952[2]. He esteemed others as viler than himself.

@975. That those in (mere) external worship are most vile; and yet may perform vile services in the Church. Treated of. @1097. @1103.

@986[3]. They are amended, in order to serve for some vile use.

@987[2]. Man, when born, is the vilest of all living (creatures).

@996. (These) delights are relatively vile; for all delight is such that it is the more vile in proportion as it verges to externals... (Thus) man's delight of pleasures, while he lives in the body, is vile relatively to his delight after (death)... nay, so vile, that good Spirits utterly spurn the delights of the body... and in like manner the delight of these Spirits becomes vile when they are elevated... into the Heaven of angelic Spirits. @3938[4].

@--[3]. "Grass," etc, = what is vilest (or lowest).

@1030[2]. The things of the external man... thus the viler things. Signified.

@--. Those not of the Church, who are more vile. Signified.

@1094. "A servant of servants" = what is lowest in the Church.

@1594[4]. He acknowledges... that he is something vile and filthy.

@1911. "Her mistress was vile in her eyes" (Genesis 16:4) = that this Rational, at its conception despised -vilipenderet- the truth itself adjoined to good. @--[6], Explained @1914. @1916.

@2890. Evil Spirits regard man as a vile slave... Explained. @SE 2924.

@3938[4]. He begins to hold in slight esteem these delights...

@3951[2]. They thus make themselves (unnecessarily) of low estimation...

@5145[6]. When (what is good and true, etc.) is regarded as relatively worthless...

@5648[3]. They (then) hold as worthless, and loathe, the spiritual things of the internal sense.

@6732. "A coffer of bulrush" = what is of low esteem, but is still derived from truth; thus that truth is of low esteem.

@7317[3]. They begin to hold cheap the doctrinals of their faith.

@8478[3]. They are not dejected if they are low in station.

@9231[end]. Their comparing themselves to "dead dogs" = that they were to be accounted as utterly worthless -vilissimis-...

@HH 158. The delight of life and of Heaven... would gradually become worthless -vilesceret- if they were continually in it.

@327[end]. They are sometimes taken out that they may serve others for... low uses.

@472[2]. Servants whom their master holds in slight esteem...

@564[end]. They who have exercised dominion from the love of self... are vile slaves in Hell.

@AR 107[8]. As they either pass by, or hold in slight esteem, the truths of doctrine...

@CL 263[end]. They sink down into a certain prison, where they are called viler than the vile, that is, the vilest.

@TCR 405. Emperors and kings... are sometimes less in (the love of rule) than those who are of low origin...

@SE 992. Such a Spirit holds cheap effects or ultimates.

@3839[end]. Spiritual things, and confirmatory natural ones, he utterly despised and nauseated as vile and null.

@AE 240[6]. "All that honoured her despise her" (Lamentations 1:8).

Village.; Villa.

@AC 2909[3]. "(Hebron) given to Caleb as to field and villages" (Joshua 21:12) = again a new Church.

@3270. "In their villages" (Genesis 25:16) = the external things of the Church... These were represented by "villages," because they were outside the cities.

@LJ 27. When man passes from the natural world into the Spiritual World, it is like passing from a village into a great city.

@CL 49. Matrimony is contracted within the region, city, or village...

@77[2]. We saw... villages and villages, with gardens, groves, and fields between them.

@TCR 119[2]. A cloud... which hides fields, villages, and cities.

@124[end]. (At the Last Judgment, the Lord) deluged their cities, villages, and fields. @SE 5094. @5283. @5359. @5366.

@AE 405[12]. "Villages" (Isaiah 42:2) = natural Knowledges and scientifics. @730[29].

Villain.; Furcifer. @TCR 672.

Villainy. See <Disgrace>.

Vine.; Arbor vini.

@DLW 346[end]. The less perfect (plants) are vines and shrubs.

Vine.; Vitis.

@AC 217. "A vine," in the Word, = spiritual good. Illustrated.

@886[2]. "Thy wife like a fruitful vine" (Psalms 128:3) = the Spiritual Church.

@1069[4]. As "a vineyard" = the Spiritual Church, so does "a vine," because a vine belongs to a vineyard... Illustrated. @1071[2]. @2702[14].

@--[5]. As "a vine" = the Spiritual Church, and as charity is the primary of the Spiritual Church, in which primary the Lord is present, and through which He conjoins Himself with man, and through which He alone operates all good, the Lord compares Himself to "a vine," and describes the man of the Church, or the Spiritual Church, in these words: "I am the true Vine, and My Father is the Vine-dresser, every branch in Me that beareth not fruit, He taketh away... I am the Vine, ye are the branches..." (John 15:1-5, 12).

@1462[end]. The Lord is called "a vine out of Egypt" (Psalms 80:8) as to the Knowledges in which He was instructed.

@2240[8]. "A vine" is predicated of truths and of falsities... thus "the vine of Sodom" (Deuteronomy 32:32) = falsity from evil.

@2722[7]. Groves of olives = the celestial things of worship; groves of vines, its spiritual things...

@2781[5]. "Vine," and "noble vine" (Genesis 49:11) = the Spiritual Church external and internal.

@2834. The adoption of the spiritual is described in... "I am the Vine, ye are the branches..." "A vine" = the Spiritual Church.

@3142[2]. "A vine out of Egypt" = truth from scientifics.

@3579[2]. "The vine shall give her fruit" (Zechariah 8:12) = that the Spiritual of the Church - that is, the truth of faith - will give good.

@3941[8]. "The vine and fig" (Deuteronomy 8:8) = the goods of faith (as distinguished from the goods of love).

@4013[3]. Some species of trees = interior goods and truths, which are of the spiritual (as distinguished from the natural) man, such as olives and vines.

@4552[3]. In the Ancient Church... the vine, and the derivative wine = the things which are of charity, and of the faith from this.

@4599[2]. "A noble vine" (Isaiah 5:2) = spiritual good. ( = the good of faith of the Spiritual Church. @9139[4].)

@5113. "Lo a vine before me" (Genesis 40:9) = the Intellectual of the Spiritual Church. @--[4], Illustrated.

@--[4]. "A noble vine" (Jeremiah 2:21) = the man of the Spiritual Church, who is called "a vine" from what is intellectual. "The degenerate branches of a strange vine" (Jeremiah 2:21) = the man of a perverted Church.

@--[5]. Its becoming "a luxuriant vine," and "a vine of magnificence" (Ezekiel 17:6, 8) = becoming a Spiritual Church, which is called "a vine" from the derivative wine, signifying spiritual good, or the good of charity, from which is the truth of faith implanted in the intellectual part. ( = the external and internal Spiritual Church. @8764[6].) @AE 281[2].

@--[10]. "The vine" (Genesis 49:11) = the Intellectual which is of the Spiritual Church; and "the noble vine" = the Intellectual which is of the Celestial Church.

@--[11]. "A vine out of Egypt," in the supreme sense, = the Lord; the glorification of His Human being described by it and its branches. In the internal sense, "a vine," here, = the Spiritual Church, and the man of this Church, such as he is when... regenerated as to the Intellectual and the Voluntary. @9341[2].

@--[13]. "A vine" = the good of the Intellectual... or, what is the same, the good of the interior man. Illustrated.

@--[14]. That "a vine" = the Intellectual made new, or regenerated, through good from truth, and through truth from good. Illustrated. (These) are signified by "the fruit of the vine-genimen vitis" (Matthew 26:29).

@--[15]. As the Intellectual of the spiritual man is... regenerated through the truth which is from the Lord alone, the Lord compares Himself to "a Vine"; and those who are being implanted in the truth which is from Him, and consequently in Him, He compares to "the branches;" and the derivative good, to "the fruit."

@--[16]. As, in the supreme sense, "a vine" = the Lord as to Divine truth; and, from this, in the internal sense, the man of the Spiritual Church, "a vineyard" = the Spiritual Church itself.

@--[17]. See <Nazarite>.

@5114. "And in the vine three shoots" (Genesis 40:10) = the derivative derivations down to the ultimate one. "A vine" = the Intellectual. Explained.

@5117[4]. "No grapes in the vine" (Jeremiah 8:13) = no interior or rational good.

@6375. "He binds his young donkey to the vine" (Genesis 49:11) = (conjunction through) truth in the Natural for the external Church... "A vine" = the Spiritual Church; here, the external Spiritual Church, because "a choice vine" = the internal Church. @AE 433[4].

@6376. "And his donkey's colt unto the choice vine" (Genesis 49:11) = (through) truth from the Rational for the internal Church. Explained. @AE 433[4].

@6432[6]. "A vine" = the Spiritual Church, and consequently the good of truth. References.

@7553[5]. "A vine" (Psalms 105:33) = the truth and good of the internal Church.

@8408[end]. "Gourds -colocynthides- from a wild vine" (2 Kings 4:39) = falsification. ( = falsities. @10105[3].)

@9052[4]. "A vine" = the Spiritual Church.

@9139[5]. To "vintage the vine of the earth" (Revelation 14:18) = to consume the truth and good of the Church. (Compare @AC 5113[2], @AR 649, and @AE 918.)

@--[end]. The Lord called Himself "a Vine" (because) "a vine" = faith in the Lord, and consequently the Lord as to faith; for the Lord is faith because faith is from Him...

@9277[3]. "A vine" (Habakkuk 3:17) = spiritual good.

@--[4]. "A vine" = the good of the Spiritual Church.

@9320[3]. "A vine" = the Church. References.

@9325[5]. "A vine" = the truth and good of the Spiritual Church.

@10137[4]. "A vine" = the interior good of the Spiritual Church.

@10261[7]. "A vine" = a Church which is in spiritual good.

@--[8]. "A vine" = the good of the internal Spiritual church.

@10402[5]. References.

@DSS 18[3]. The olive, the vine, the cedar, etc. = the celestial, spiritual, rational, etc. good and truth of the Church.

@23[2]. An olive = the good of love; a vine, truth from this good.

@AR 875[4]. (A garden seen which contained vines, etc. in order.)

@--[15]. An olive (seen) the trunk of which was entwined with a vine.

@936[end]. The leaves of an olive and of a vine = rational truths from celestial and spiritual light.

@CL 13. Trees twined round with tendrilled vines, seen. @75[2].

@183. Between olive and olive, running and pendulous vines.

@TCR 348[2]. Faith without Truths is like a vine which bears wild grapes.

@609[end]. Silver, a sapphire, and a vine, in the Word, = spiritual good, which is the good of the Middle Heaven.

@708[end]. "The fruit of the vine" = the truth of the New Church and Heaven. ( = Divine truth from Divine good, and the derivative bliss and happiness. @AE 252[6].) @376[26].

@AE 175[8]. "A vine" = the internal Church, thus the internal things of the Church.

@304[39]. "The vine in the field" (Malachi 3:11) = the truths of the Church.

@323[2]. "The vine shall languish" (Isaiah 24:7) = that the truth (of the Spiritual Church) will cease... "The vine" = spiritual truth. @376[20].

@329[19]. "The vine" = the Church. @433[30].

@340[13]. "A vine" = the Spiritual Church from the affection of truth.

@357[18]. "A thousand vines" (Isaiah 7:23) = truths from good in abundance.

@365[28]. "The vine shall give its fruit" (Zechariah 8:12) = that truth will produce good... For "a vine" = the Church as to truths, or the truths of the Church.

@374[7]. "Vine and fig-tree" (Deuteronomy 8:8) = good and truth from a spiritual origin.

@375[31]. "A noble vine" (Isaiah 5:2) = spiritual truth from what is celestial, or truth from the good of love. ( = genuine truths. @918[4].)

@--[37]. "Vine" corresponds to spiritual good, which in its essence is truth.

@376[end]. "wine" = the doctrine itself (of the Spiritual, Church).

@388[4]. "Vine" = the Church as to truth, which is called the Spiritual Church. @618[7].

@--[5]. "I will lay waste her vine" (Hosea 2:12) = the internal Church which is of the spiritual man.

@391[25]. "Israel is an empty vine" (Hosea 10:1) = the Church when there is no longer any truth.

@403[2]. In general, "the vine" = the Spiritual which is of truth from good... In the spiritual sense, "the vine" = the Spiritual Church.

@--[6]. "The vine" = the internal Church.

@--[9]. "The vine" = spiritual good and truth.

@--[10]. "No produce on the vines" (Habakkuk 3:17) = no spiritual good.

@--[12]. Therefore it is said of those who are in the goods and truths of the Church, and thus in safety from evils and falsities, that "they shall sit in safety under their vine and fig-tree, and none shall make afraid." Illustrated.

@--[22]. "The vine" = the internal or spiritual things of the Church. @--[13]. @638[21].

@405[15]. "A vine out of Egypt" = the Spiritual Church, which begins with man through scientifics and Knowledges in the natural man. @518[16], Explained. @569[14].

@--. To "plant a vine" = to establish a spiritual Church.

@458[7]. "The vine" = the spiritual good and truth of the Church.

@503[4]. "The vine" = the spiritual truth of the Church. @--[5]. @717[3].

@504[27]. "Thy mother is like a vine" (Ezekiel 19:10) = the Ancient Church, which was in the good of life and the derivative truths. ( = that the Spiritual Church, from its establishment, had been instructed in truths. @727[3].)

@519[7]. "Their vine is of the vine of Sodom" (Deuteronomy 32:32) = the Church (in) all evils from the love of self.

@556[4]. "It reduces my vine to a waste" (Joel 1:7) = destroying spiritual truths, which are those of the spiritual sense of the Word.

@618[4]. "The vine" = the truth of doctrine of the Church.

@638[3]. There are three trees which principally = the Church: the olive, the vine, and the fig;... the vine = the Spiritual Church.

@--[13]. "Thy wife shall be as a fruitful vine..." = the Church as to the affection of truth.

@--[23]. "The vine" = the truth of celestial good.

@695[13]. "The vine" = the Church as to the spiritual affection of truth.

@724[24]. "Behold, and visit this vine" (Psalms 80:14) = the Spiritual Church.

@--[27]. "Vine and fig-tree" = an internal and external Spiritual Church. @911[14].

@911[10]. "The vine of Sibmah" = the Church (formed of men of the external Church who explain the Word to favour worldly loves).

@1145[2]. The wood of the vine = spiritual good.

Vinedresser.; Vinitor.

@AC 1069[5]. See <Vine>.

@AE 374[4]. "The vine-dressers that howled for the wheat and barley" (Joel 1:11) = those who are of the Church. ( = those who are in truths, and teach them. @376[18]. @911[13].)

Vinegar.; Acetum.
See <Sour>.

@DLord 16[6]. That they offered Him vinegar to drink = things merely falsified and false; and therefore He did not drink it; and then said, "It is consummated." (Compare @AR 410[end].) @TCR 130[end].

@TCR 38[2]. Like... worms swimming in vinegar.

@132[3]. As from a cask of vinegar nothing but vinegar comes.

@AE 386[30]. That "vinegar" was given Him (John 19:29) = that in the coming Church there would be no genuine truth, but truth mixed with falsities, such as there is with those who separate faith from charity, or truth from good. This is what "vinegar" signifies.

@519[2]. Their giving to the Lord "vinegar mingled with gall" (Matthew 27:34) which was also called "wine mingled with myrrh" (Mark 15:23) = what Divine truth from the Word was with the Jewish nation; namely, that it was mingled with the falsity of evil, and was thus wholly falsified and adulterated, and therefore He would not drink it. But that afterwards they gave the Lord "vinegar in a sponge, and placed it upon a hyssop-stalk" (Matthew 27:48; Mark 15:36; John 19:29) = the kind of falsity there was among the upright gentiles, which was falsity from ignorance of the truth, in which there was what is good and useful; and as this falsity is accepted by the Lord, He drank this vinegar. The hyssop-stalk upon which they placed it = the purification of the falsity. (Compare @627[end].)

Vineyard.; Vinea.
See <Vine>.

@AC 1069. "Noah planted a vineyard" (Genesis 9:20) = the derivative Church. That "a vineyard" = a Spiritual Church. Explained, Illustrated. @2702[14]. @4599[2]. @5113[16]. @5117[2]. @--[3]. To "plant vineyards" = to be instructed in the truths and goods of faith. Illustrated.

@1306[end]. When the Lord's Church is compared to "a vineyard," the things which are of worship, and also of its preservation, are compared to "a winepress," and "a tower in a vineyard". Illustrated.

@2027[3]. Some of them say that they have laboured in the Lord's vineyard...

@3220. Under <Vegetable>, see this reference.

@3820[4]. They who labour in the Lord's vineyard, obtain a reward everyone according to the affection of good and truth from which he labours...

@3941[3]. "Vineyard," and "field" = the Church.

@4592[2]. "The house of the vineyard," or "Beth Kerem" (Jeremiah 6:1) = the Spiritual Church.

@5117[7]. To "sit and plant vineyards" (Amos 9:14) = to cultivate the things of the Spiritual Church.

@9139. To "lay waste a field or vineyard" (Exodus 22:5) = the deprivation of the good and truth of the Church through cupidities... "A vineyard" = the Church as to truth, thus the truth of the Church. This is because wine, which is of the vineyard, = the truth of good.

@--[2]. This signification of "a vineyard" originates from the representatives in the Spiritual World; for... there appear vineyards full of grapes, with winepresses in them, when the Angels are in discourse about a company of people who are in the truth of good.

@--[3]. That "a vineyard" = the Church as to the good and truth of faith, which is called the Spiritual Church. Illustrated. @9277.

@9142. "A vineyard" (Exodus 22:5) = the truth of the Church.

@9277. "Thy vineyard" (Exodus 23:11) = spiritual good, which is the good of charity towards the neighbour; for this good makes the Spiritual Church.

@--[3]. "Vineyards" (Amos 4:9) = the goods of faith. ( = spiritual goods and truths. @AE 403[8].)

@10184[6]. "A vineyard" = the Church with man; "the produce of a vineyard" = a state of truth.

@10669. "A vineyard" = the Church as to truth.

@HH 489. [Swedenborg footnote 1.] "A vineyard" = the Spiritual Church, and the truths of this Church. References.

@520[end]. The ways which lead to the Spiritual Kingdom appear adorned with vines and laurels, because vines and laurels correspond to the affection of truth and its uses.

@AR 132[2]. To "take away the vineyard from Naboth, and kill him" (1 Kings 21) = to take away and kill the Church itself; for "a vineyard" = the Church. Compare @AE 160[2].

@315. "Vineyard" = the Church as to truth and the derivative good.

@316[4]. Hence a "vineyard," in the Word, = a Church which is in truths from the Lord.

@647[2]. "The vineyard of the earth" (Revelation 14:18) = the Church in the Christian world, @649, Explained. (Compare @AE 918.)

@649[end]. "A vineyard" = the Church where there is the Divine truth of the Word, and the Lord is known by it; because "wine" = interior truth, which is from the Lord through the Word; and therefore "a vineyard," here, = the Christian Church. @650, Illustrated. @651.

@AE 194[2]. The parable of the labourers in the vineyard (Matthew 20.) Explained.

@--. To "labour in the vineyard" = to procure for one's self spiritual life by the Knowledges of good and truth from the Word being applied to the uses of life.

@--. "A vineyard" = the Spiritual Church, and spiritual life with man. References.

@315[2]. The parable of the man who planted a vineyard (Luke 20). Explained. @922[7].

@--. "The vineyard" which the man planted = a Church which is in truths.

@375[31]. "The vineyard which the beloved had in a horn of a son of oil" (Isaiah 5:1) = the Spiritual Church, which has truths from the good of love, thus most excellent ones; for "a vineyard" = the Spiritual Church, that is, the Church which is in truths from good. @918[4].

@376[6]. "A vineyard" = the Spiritual Church; and therefore "vineyards" = all things of the Church.

@--[end]. "A vineyard" = the Spiritual Church, that is, the Church which is in the truths and goods of doctrine from the Word.

@386[21]. To "plant vineyards" (Psalms 107:37) = to receive truths in the understanding, that is, in spirit; for "vineyards" = spiritual truths, and therefore to "plant them" = to receive them spiritually, that is, to understand them.

@388[3]. "Many shepherds have destroyed My vineyard" (Jeremiah 12:10) = the vastation of the Church as to its truths. @730[8].

@403[20]. "The vineyard in which was the fig-tree" (Luke 13:6) = the Church, where are also those who are in externals. Explained... For "a vineyard" = the internal of the Church; and "a fig-tree," its external.

@433[34]. "My vineyard" (Isaiah 5:4) = the Church with that nation. @594[11], Described. @632[7].

@449[7]. "The house of the vineyard" (Jeremiah 6:1) = that Church itself.

@617[12]. To "plant vineyards and eat the fruit of them" (Isaiah 65:21) = to enrich themselves with spiritual truths, and to appropriate to themselves the derivative goods.

@--[13]. "A vineyard" = the Church as to truths. @734[12].

@638[20]. "Vineyards" = the spiritual or interior truths of the Church.

@650[53]. "A vineyard" = the Spiritual Church, that is, the Church as to the affection of truth.

@706[17]. To "plant vineyards" = the implantation of truth, and its reception.

@918[9]. "A vineyard" = the Spiritual Church.

Vinous. See <Wine>.

Vintage.; Vindemia.
Vintage, To.; Vindemiare.
Vintaging, A.; Vindemiatio.
Grape-gatherer.; Vindemiator.

@AC 5117[11]. To "vintage the clusters of the earth" (Revelation 14:18) = to destroy all things of charity. ( = to consume the truth and good of the Church. @9139[3].) (Compare @AR 649. @650.)

@5135[8]. "Grape-gatherers" (Obadiah 1:5) = falsities which are not from evil. @AE 919[5].

@AR 650. To vintage, is to take down the vine and gather the grapes.

@AE 313[12]. "Vintage" = the truth of the Church.

@376[14]. The truths of good that were taken away, are meant by "the vintage..." (Jeremiah 48:32).

@555[20]. "The vintage that shall be consumed..." (Isaiah 32:10) = no longer any truth of the Church; for "vintage" = the same as "wine," namely, the truth of the Church.

@638[18]. Spiritual good, which is truth from celestial good, is signified by "the vintage;" and vastation is signified by "the beating," and "the gleanings, when the vintage is done" (Isaiah 24:13).

@918. To "put in the sharp sickle, and vintage" (Revelation 14:18) = to gather together the good, and separate them from the evil. Explained. @919.

@919. To "vintage" = to collect for uses things which will be of service to the understanding, and will give intelligence and wisdom; and, in the opposite sense, to devastate the Church as to spiritual good, and thus as to the understanding and affection of truth. "Vintage," and to "vintage," are used in this opposite sense when there are no longer any clusters or grapes remaining; by which, in the spiritual sense, is signified that all spiritual good, and thus all truth which in itself is truth, has been destroyed...

@--[2]. Therefore "vintaging" = devastation. Illustrated.

@922[5]. "Bozrah" means "vintaging."

@--[end]. "Vintage" = the good of spiritual love, which is love towards the neighbour.

Violence.; Violentia.
Violate. Do Violence to.; Violare.
Violation.; Violatio.
Violator.; Violator.
Violent, The.; Violenti.
Violently.; Violenter.
See <Blood>.

@AC 621. "Filled with violence" (Genesis 6:11) = their filthy cupidities. @623.

@--[end]. "Violence" is predicated of the things of the will, when vastated. @623[2].

@623. It is called "violence," when men inflict violence on holy things, by profaning them. Illustrated.

@--. The violent. Treated of.

@632. "The earth is filled with violence" (verse 13) = that they no longer had the will of good.

@1005. That violence inflicted on charity will punish itself. Signified, Explained.

@--. "Blood" = violence inflicted on charity. Illustrated.

@1476. That thus the Celestial could not be violated. Signified, Explained.

@1496. That thus the truth which was to be conjoined with the Celestial might have been violated. Signified, Explained.

@2053[2]. Truths of conscience are various... and the Lord wills not to do violence to them. Explained.

@2357. Lest they should do violence to the good of charity. Signified, Explained.

@2359. Lest they should do violence to the good of charity and the Lord's Divine Human and proceeding Divine. Signified, Explained. @2365.

@2967[4]. "The violent ones of the nations" (Ezekiel 28:7) = evils that destroy goods. @AE 388[12]. @537[16].

@4299[3]. Evils, falsities, and unmercifulness continually strive to do violence to these holy things...

@4502[2]. "Instruments of violence are their swords" (Genesis 49:5) = falsities and evils which inflicted violence on truths and goods. ( = that the doctrinal things serve to destroy the works of charity, thus charity itself. @6353.)

@6353. That "violence" = the destruction of charity.

@--[4]. That "violence" = force put upon charity. Illustrated.

@7047. That it was full of violence and hostility towards truth and good. Signified, Explained.

@7317. Violence done to Divine truth. Signified.

@7326. Violence inflicted on charity, also on faith, and thus on the holy truth which proceeds from the Lord. Signified. Violence is inflicted on it when it is falsified.

@7502[3]. There is such an order in Heaven from the Lord, that nothing is done violently; but all things in freedom.

@8187. The endeavour to inflict violence by an influx of falsity from evil. Signified, Explained.

@8284. The endeavour, with the evil, to inflict violence. Signified, Explained.

@8575. That they are not far from inflicting violence on truth from the Divine. Signified, Explained.

@8625. Because they want to inflict violence on the Lord's Spiritual Kingdom. Signified, Explained.

@8887. To "sanctify it" = no violation in any way. Explained.

@--. The Sabbath not to be violated in any way. @8895.

@9127. That he is not guilty of the violence which has been inflicted. Signified, Explained.

@--. To inflict violence on truth Divine, that is, on the truth of good, and also on good itself. Signified. For he who inflicts violence on truth, inflicts violence on good also. Explained.

@9132. He is guilty of the violence inflicted on (good and truth). Signified, Explained.

@9250. To be "a witness of violence" (Exodus 23:1) = no affirmation of such things as are contrary to the good of charity.

@--. "Violence" = the destruction of the good of charity.

@10287[10]. "Violent men" (Psalms 54:3) = (evils and falsities) which inflict violence on goods and truths.

@HH 384[end]. A perpetual endeavour to dissolve and do violence to marriages.

@514[end]. The laws of religion (to be) in no way violated in the deeds.

@DLord 14[2]. The Word, to which violence had been done. Signified.

@DSS 26. If a man is in the knowledge of correspondences, he can do violence to the spiritual sense.

@DP 231[3]. He who confirms evil loves inflicts violence on Divine goods; and he who confirms false principles inflicts violence on Divine truths: the latter violence is called the falsification of truth, and the former the adulteration of good. Both are meant by "bloods."

@AR 316. Lest the holy goods and truths which lie hidden interiorly in the Word, be violated and profaned. Signified, Explained.

@653. Violence inflicted on the Word by direful falsifications of truth. Signified, Explained.

@675[end]. The bishop cried, Violence! violence! @TCR 389[end].

@825. Divine truth in the ultimate sense... to which violence has been done. Signified, Explained.

@CL 511. On the lust of violation. General article. @SE 6110[4].

@--. These violators. Described. @512.

@512[end]. This is not from any lust of violation.

@515. On the correspondence of whoredoms with the violation of spiritual marriage. Explained.

@TCR 74[3]. God never violates man's free will...

@SE 391. On the torment of those who use violence against others. Explained.

@2688. That he who lives in faith in the Lord... cannot possibly suffer violence from the evil. Explained.

@2888. That ability -copia- to resist the evil, even with violence, is granted. Explained.

@4298. On the penalty of those who want to do violence to infants.

@5493. He had forcibly violated many.

@--[end]. Where there are filthinesses from adulteries and violations.

@5669. On the sphere of violation.

@--. This is meant, in the internal sense, by "the violation of virgins," and by "the violent," in the Word.

@5996. On a cadaverous breast from the violation of marriage. Explained.

@6106[2]. Some men, who love violations... want the wives to fight their husbands...

@AE 175[10]. "Full of violence" (Ezekiel 7:23) = puts force on the good of charity.

@279[4]. To "draw to them the habitation of violence" (Amos 6:3) = to live a life contrary to charity.

@328[13]. To "redeem out of the hand of the violent" (Jeremiah 15:20) = to deliver from the falsities which offer violence to the good of charity. "The violent" = these falsities, and therefore those who are in them.

@329[18]. "He shall redeem their soul from deceit and violence" (Psalms 72:14) = deliverance from the evils and falsities which destroy the goods of love and truths of faith.

@365[41]. "Violence shall no more be heard in thy land ..." (Isaiah 60:18) = there shall no longer be disagreement between the spiritual and natural man. "Violence" = disagreement.

@481[3]. "The blast of the violent ones" (Isaiah 25:4) = things contrary to the goods and truths of the Church. Those are called "the violent" who endeavour to destroy goods and truths...

@650[64]. "The violence of Lebanon" (Habakkuk 2:17) = force put upon the truths perceived by the rational man from the Word.

@--. "The violence of the land, of the city, and of all that dwell in it" (Habakkuk 2:17) = force put, by means of falsities, upon the truths and goods of the Church, and upon its doctrine...

@654[72]. "Violence to the sons of Judah..." (Joel 3:19) = violence to the truths and goods of the Word. ( = the adulteration of the Word as to good. @730[20].)

@659[5]. To those who have perceived delight in violating women, there is nothing more delightful than a cadaverous stink.

@734[17]. He is called "a man of violences" (Psalms 140:4) who, with a wicked purpose, inflicts violence on the truths of the Word by perverting them. @750[20]. @866[4].

@922[5]. The Word in the letter on which violence has been inflicted by adulterations and falsifications of it. Signified.

@991[end]. The desire of violating... then perishes.

@1006[2]. There are cadaverous Hells for those to whom violations of wives had been delightful.

Violin.; Viol. Violina.

@SE 1996. See <Instrument>. @4482.

Viper.; Echidna.

@CL 79[4]. Hydras and vipers, seen.

@Coro 38[end]. They called them Lernaean Hydras.

Viper.; Vipera.

@AC 259[2]. See <Serpent>. @6398[end]. @9013[3].

@2125. A tree of knowledge seen with a great viper in it. @SE 3993.

@4533[2]. The most deceitful appear as vipers. @CL 514[3].

@5608[7]. "The sucking child shall play on the hole of the viper" (Isaiah 11:8)... "Vipers" = those who are most deceitful. @AE 314[3]. @410[9]. @581[5].

@9013[6]. Falsity lies hidden in the truths they speak, and evil in the goods they do - which is concealed poison - hence they are called "an offspring of vipers" (Matthew 12:34). @AE 581[5].

@HH 578. Genii scatter evils round as vipers do poison.

@579[end]. When they are inspected as to their deceit and cunning, they appear like vipers.

@AR 624[end]. The deceitful are signified in the Word by ... "vipers;" and the deceit by their "poison."

@CL 264. The ankles of (the devil's) feet were like two vipers.

@TCR 489. Predestination, that horrible viper.

@533. Like vipers hidden in a rock full of holes.

@SE 5498. In the Hell of assassins and poisoners, there appear... lower down, as it were dragons and vipers, because they flatter before they infuse their poison.

@5692. (The cunning and deceitful) are sensuous, and are serpents, but especially poisonous ones, and vipers; and so do they appear in the light of Heaven.

@6098[end]. (That bishop) afterwards appeared like a viper.

@AE 581[4]. "A viper is hatched" (Isaiah 59:5). Explained.

@--[5]. "The hole of the viper" = the Hells in which are deceitful and cunning Spirits, the entrances to which appear like dusky holes.

@654[41]. "The viper, and flying fire-serpent" (Isaiah 30:6) = what is sensuous reasoning cunningly and craftily.

Virgin.; Virgo.
Virginity.; Virginitas.
Virgin.; Virgineus.
See <Mary>.

@AC 54[end]. The Church itself, from the affection of good, is called... "virgin." @253.

@828. On those who desire nothing more than to deflower virgins, and to whom virginities, and thefts of virginities are the greatest delight. (Their frightful punishment described.) @SE 2704, General article. @DeConj 126.

@--. For it is the first flower of love which introduces virgins into chaste conjugial love, and conjoins the minds of the married partners.

@1414. He was born of a virgin mother, and by birth He derived infirmities from the virgin mother... @1428.

@1644[end]. The speech of angelic Spirits was represented by a virgin...

@2296. Infants seen with their virgin educatresses.

@2362[4]. The Celestial Church, being from love to the Lord in love towards the neighbour, is likened to an unmarried daughter, or virgin... as in "These are they who have not been defiled with women, for they are virgins..." (Revelation 14:4). And that this might be represented in the Jewish Church, it was enjoined upon the priests that they should marry... virgins (Leviticus 21:13-15; Ezekiel 44:22).

@2735. Genuine conjugial love... is represented by a virgin of inexpressible beauty encompassed with a bright cloud...

@2753. There are some who are possessed by the cupidity of seducing virgins... (Their lot.)

@2762[4]. The virgins (of Parnassus) were knowledges. @4966[2]. @7729[end]. ( = cognitions and scientifics of every kind). @CL 182[2]. @DeVerbo 7[3].

@3079[end]. "(The ten) virgins" = affections.

@3081. "A virgin, and a man had not Known her" (Genesis 24:16) = pure from everything false.

@--. "A virgin," in the Word, = the Lord's Kingdom, and also the Church, and therefore everyone who is a Kingdom of the Lord, or a Church; and this from the conjugial love which is in chaste virgins. Illustrated.

@--[3]. In the proper sense, those are "virgins" who are in love to the Lord, that is, the celestial; and thus those who are in the affection of good. Those, also, are called "virgins" who are in charity towards the neighbour, that is, the spiritual, thus those who are in the affection of truth. Illustrated.

@--[7]. The term "virgin" is used in distinction from "damsel" to express innocence. "Virgins" are so called from conjugial love, and thus mean those who are in innocence...

@3164[2]. "A betrothed virgin" = the truth of the Church about to be conjoined with good.

@3325[6]. "Virgins" = the good of love to the Lord and of charity towards the neighbour; thus those who are in innocence.

@4638. (The parable of the ten virgins) = the last time of the old Church, and the first of the new... "The ten virgins" = all in the Church, both those in good and truth, and those in evil and falsity, (The parable Fully explained.) @8989[8]. @DSS 7. Fully explained.

@4844[16]. The "virgins" whom the priests were to marry = the affection of truth.

@4966[2]. The three virgins called the Graces = affections of good; and the virgins called Heliconidae and Parnassidae [or the Muses] = affections of truth.

@5391. The chaste virgins of the renal capsules. Described. @SE 970.

@6742. "A virgin" = the good which is of the Celestial Church; but "a girl," the truth of good, which is of the Spiritual Church. Illustrated.

@7668[4]. "Beautiful virgins" (Amos 8:13) = the affection of truth. ( = those in affections of good. @8568.) ( = affections of truth from good. @AE 386[11].)

@8337[3]. "The virgin of Israel" (Jeremiah 31:4) = the Spiritual Church.

@9182. "If... a man shall persuade a virgin who is not betrothed" (Exodus 22:16) = good not conjoined with truth. Explained.

@9369. Those in persuasive faith... are meant by "the five foolish virgins, who had no oil in their lamps."

@HH 368[end]. "A virgin," and "a woman," in the Word, = the affection of good.

@DSS 17[3]. As "virgins" = those who are of the Church, there are so frequently mentioned in the Prophetic Word "the virgin," and "daughter," "of Zion," "of Jerusalem," and "of Israel."

@23. The images of virgins (with the Ancients) signified affections of truth.

@26[5]. The modest virgins (seen in a representative vision) signified affections of truth.

@DP 328[9]. They who have acknowledged truths with the lips, but not with the heart, are like the foolish virgins, who had lamps but no oil...

@AR 620. "Those not defiled with women, for they are virgins" (Revelation 14:4) = that they have not adulterated the truths of the Church, and defiled them with falsities of faith; but that they have loved truths because they are truths... thus from spiritual affection... The reason these are meant by "virgins," is that "a virgin" = the Church as a bride, which wants to be conjoined with the Lord, and to become a wife; and a Church which wants to be conjoined with the Lord, loves truths because they are truths; for the conjunction is effected by means of truths when they are lived. Hence it is that Israel, Zion, and Jerusalem... are called "virgins," and "daughters." ( = because they are in the affection of truth for the sake of truth. @AE 863.)

@620[2]. That all such in the Lord's Church... are meant by "virgins," Illustrated.

@--[3]. Like affections are signified by "virgins" in other passages, where "young men" are mentioned with them, because "young men" = truths; and "virgins," the affections of them. Illustrated.

@CL 20[2]. Six virgins (seen at a wedding in Heaven).

@21[3]. (No men stood beside the bridegroom, because on the wedding-day the men) are numbered among the virgins... Virgins = the Church, which is of both sexes; and therefore men, as well as women, as to the Church, are virgins. Illustrated.

@22. (The six virgins could not endure the close approach of the visitors.) Explained.

@--[2]. The Angel said. In Heaven we love virgins for their beauty and the grace of their manners, and we love them very much, but chastely.

@42[end]. When (the angelic pair) came near their Heaven, virgins came to meet them, received, and introduced them.

@44[2]. In Heaven there are virgins and youths, virgins of such beauty that they may be called beauties in beauty's own form... and the beauties of the virgins, and the moralities of the youths, correspond to each other... @355[2]. @381.

@--[4]. All novitiates, on ascending into Heaven... are introduced into the company of virgins, the beauties of Heaven, who perceive from their tone of voice, speech, faces, eyes, gestures, and outpouring sphere, of what quality they are in respect to the love of the sex. Described.

@--[5]. Within the enclosure of the heart, and above it, the morality of a youth is deliciated with the beauty of a virgin with the deliciousnesses of the chaste love of the sex...

@--[6]. Love truly conjugial comes into existence when a youth sees a virgin who has been provided by the Lord, and the virgin sees the youth...

@55. (Wives and virgins heard singing in Heaven.) Described.

@155[3]. Whether those who have... vowed perpetual virginity are received into Heaven, Explained.

@187[2]. There then arises the conjugial inclination, which is that of a virgin for a youth, and of a youth for a virgin; and, as the virgins in Heaven, equally as on earth, from innate prudence conceal their inclination to marriage, the youths there (suppose) that they affect the virgins with love...

@199. Thus is a virgin formed into a wife. Explained.

@207[6]. Some of these are called... the sports of the virgins of the fountain, because virgins = the affections of knowledges; and everyone has intelligence according to his affection of knowledges.

@--[end]. There (then) came some virgins with pieces of embroidery and knitting, the works of their own hands, which they gave (the three strangers). And after they were gone, the virgins sang an ode...

@293[6]. The little boy said. Read this before these virgins of the fountain... I asked them. Why did he call you the virgins of the fountain (seeing that they were wives)? They replied, We are called virgins when we are sitting by this fountain, because we are the affections of the Truths of the wisdom of our husbands; and the affection of truth is called a virgin.

@384. In the virgins (of Heaven) there is only the brightness-of beauty; but in the wives its splendour.

@460. Provided (the pellicacy) is not with a virgin...

@--. For, with women, conjugial love acts as a one with their virginity... and therefore to solemnly promise and surrender that virginity to any man, is to give a pledge that she will love him to eternity; and therefore a virgin cannot bargain it away with any rational consent, except with the solemn promise of the conjugial covenant. It is also the crown of her honour. Therefore, to take it from her without the covenant of marriage, and then discard her, is to make a harlot of some virgin who might have become a bride and a chaste wife, or to defraud some other man... Therefore he who joins to him a virgin as a mistress, may indeed cohabit with her, and thus initiate her into the friendship of love; but with the constant intention... that she shall become his wife.

@477[6]. Virgins, who were beauties, because images of heavenly affection, were brought to (the novitiate Spirit)... but on seeing them he returned into his internals, and... they vanished. Explained.

@502. On the state of a virgin... before marriage, and after it. Explained.

@503. That virginity is the crown of chastity, and the pledge of conjugial love. Explained.

@504. Some adulterers are possessed with the desire of deflowering virgins...

@--. When (their) potency has failed, they boast of the number of virginities...

@--[end]. If (such marry) they have nothing in mind but the virginity of their future consort; and, when they have sipped this, they loathe both bed and chamber.

@TCR 106. The first state (of regeneration) is represented by... that of every virgin before she becomes a wife.

@719[3]. Those who only understand and speak truths and goods, are like the foolish virgins... But those who also will and do them, are the prudent virgins...

@SE 1070. On whoremongers who with deceit allure virgins to whoredom.

@2704. On those who are possessed with a cupidity for virginities. General article.

@3017. A (representative) virgin seen. Described.

@3597[end]. Such are represented, also, by a bright virgin...

@3896. Spirits who, in life, had burned for the innocent, such as chaste virgins. Described.

@4377. A tranquil combat of the virgin -virginei- sex against the evil. Explained.

@4756. Those who have ruined virgins... are sent into such cities. Ties.

@5160. Daughters and virgins as seen in the Celestial Kingdom. Described.

@5601[end]. The virgins are admonished by changes of beauty in their faces.

@5618. On some virgins who read daily in the Word. Described.

@5660. How virgins are brought up in the other life, and in Heaven. General article.

@6042[2]. These are like the live (foolish) virgins...

@6110[52]. Virgins who have imbued piety to the extent of becoming somewhat melancholy, make sad wives, and cannot be among the happy in Heaven... Thus [is it] with those who have lived in nunneries.

@DMin 4777. In a dream, I saw a virgin in a room... She appeared like an angelic virgin; (but) she communicated with Societies of adultery. (She represented the [selfish] love of friendship.)

@AE 187[4]. "The ten virgins" = all who are of the Church; "five" = some of them... "The five wise virgins" = those who are in love and the derivative faith; and "the five foolish virgins" = those who are in no love, but in faith alone. @212[4]. @250[7]. @252[8], Fully Explained. @375[41]. @548[3]. @675[6]. @840[3]. @860.

@219[3]. "The virgin of Israel" = the Church. @555[4]. ( = the Church from the affection of truth. @863[12].)

@270[2]. "Virgins" = the affection of truth and good. @--[5]. @315[7]. @637[11].

@--[4]. "Virgins" = the spiritual affection of truth.

@275[4]. "Young men" = truths; "virgins," goods. @721[3].

@406[11]. "Young men" = affections of truth; "virgins," affections of good.

@655[6]. "The virgins in the cities of Judah" (Lamentations 5:11) = affections of truth from the good of love.

@811[3]. "A virgin" = the affection of truth.

@863. "Virgins" = those affections of truth which are called spiritual affections of truth. Explained... Those in these affections love truths because they are truths... and those who love truths in this way, love the Lord; because the Lord is in man in the truths which are from good...

@--[2]. The reason those in the spiritual affection of truth are called "virgins," is based on the marriage of good and truth, from which comes conjugial love... for as virgins love to be conjoined with men who have the understanding of truth = they = the affections of truth. Fully illustrated.

@--[8]. "Young man, and virgin" (Jeremiah 51:22) = the understanding and the affection of what is false.

@--[13]. As the Church is the Church from the spiritual affection of truth... the expressions "virgin of Israel," "the virgin daughter of Zion," "the virgin daughter of My people," "the virgin daughter of Zidon," "the virgin daughter of Egypt," and also "the virgin daughter of Babylon," are frequently used in the Word.

@--[end]. Thus "virginity" = the inviolate affection of truth. II!.

@1006[2]. There are excrementitious Hells for those whose delights have been debauchings of virgins.

@1009[end]. Virgins (seen there) who had accounted whoredoms wicked because contrary to the Divine law; and also virgins who had not accounted them wicked, but still had abstained from them on account of the disrepute, which would repel suitors. These latter virgins I have seen encompassed with a dusky cloud in their descent to the lower regions; and the former with a bright light in their ascent to the higher regions.

@1029[18]. Every Church at its beginning is like a virgin; but in process of time it becomes a harlot. Explained.

@1193[2]. Approach ten maidens in order to choose one for a wife; and will you not first examine their quality...

@DeDeoSalv 37. "The virgin," from whom He was born, = the Church as to the affection of truth.

@DeDeoSalv 38. It was necessary for Him to be born from a virgin in lawful marriage with Joseph.

Virility.; Virilitas.
Virile.; Virilis.

@AC 10225. From the twentieth to the sixtieth year... is called manhood, etc. @HH 166.

@CL 75[end]. The honourable marks of virility at once failed them (when they thought of more wives than one).

@220[3]. How is the feminine principle propagated from a masculine soul?

@297[end]. The loveliness... of the female sex surpassing the male sex.

@TCR 316[end]. The virile potency (of adulterers) when they become husbands, may be compared to the blossoming of tulips...

@SE 2494. The speech (of these Spirits) is not so manly...

Virtue. See <Power-Virtus>.

Viscous. See <Sticky>.

Viscus. Viscera.; Viscus. Viscera.
See <Member>, and <Organ>.

@AC 1803. He that shall go forth out of thy bowels (Genesis 15:4) = those in love to the Lord and the neighbour. Explained.

@--[3]. "Bowels," in the Word, = love, or mercy. Explained, Illustrated.

@1879[2]. They tried to enter into the viscera of my body...

@2054[2]. The interiors of man are conjoined with his externals by means of the heart and lungs; from this all the surrounding viscera live.

@2992. When I have been speaking about the viscera... and following their connection... the Angels... led my thoughts by means of the spiritual things to which the viscera correspond... They did not think at all about the viscera...

@3294. To be "separated from the bowels" (Genesis 25:23) = the origin of truth, (because this expression is applied to birth as coming from the father). Explained.

@3347[2]. The Angels compared the faculty of thinking to the faculty of the viscera to act according to the form of the fibres...

@3630. (Thus) each of the viscera and members... corresponds to a Society in Heaven...

@4325[2]. The parts... called the viscera... take their fibres from the cerebellum. Explained.

@4926. Truths in respect to good are like the viscera and fibres... in respect to uses.

@5171. On the correspondence of the interior viscera with the Grand Man. General article. @5377, continued.

@5258[2]. "They came to their viscera" (Genesis 41:21) = interior extermination.

@6057. The interior viscera, to which the atmospheric air cannot enter, are held together in connection and form by a more subtle air, which is called ether.

@6338[2]. Unless the soul inflowed, in the universal and in the singular, into the viscera of the body, nothing ordinate and regular could come forth in the body...

@8875[3]. "The yearning -commotio- of the bowels" (Isaiah 63:15) = mercy.

@9276[6]. The rest of the viscera and members in the Grand Man (that is, those exclusive of the heart and lungs) are constituted of those who are in external goods and truths...

@10030. That the viscera (enumerated.) = such things as are of the Spiritual World...

@10031[2]. "My bowels are troubled" (Lamentations 2:11) = grief on account of the destruction of the truth of innocence.

@10044[9]. The skin is the ultimate; the heart is the inmost; and the viscera are the intermediates or interiors. Explained.

@DLW 190[2]. Three discrete degrees in the viscera. (See <Organ>.)

@TCR 154[3]. So it is with the action of the heart in the viscera, and into the viscera, of the whole body. The heart sends out the blood in all directions, but each of the viscera takes its share according to the quality of its use.

@SE 1121. An arcanum is, that whatever any viscus, or part of a viscus, even the smallest, requires for its nourishment... it must have from the universal body. (Explained.)

@1129[end]. (Thus) the viscera of the body draw to themselves, by a species of attraction, everything that is suitable for them.

@2839[end]. (Thus) the operations of the internal viscera, which are called natural, do not require the immediate aid of Spirits, because they are according to order.

@4473. Attempt of a Siren to enter into my viscera according to my knowledges.

@AE 44[14]. "(The Samaritan) was moved with compassion -visceribus commotus est-" (Greek, εδπλαγχνιδθη) (Luke 10:33) = mercy and charity from within; for mercy and charity make a one.

@519[9]. "In the bowels" (Job 20:14) = interiorly.

@622. As "the belly," like the rest of the viscera, is within or in the midst of the body, "the belly," and also "the viscera," in the Word, = interior things. Illustrated. @--[10].

@--[10]. As "the viscera," or "bowels" = the interiors of the thought, and these are what are affected with grief, therefore this grief is expressed in the Word by the expression to be "moved in the bowels." Illustrated.

@--[13]. The reason... "the bowels" = the interiors of the thought, that is, of the understanding. Explained.

@710[11]. "From the bowels of my mother" (Isaiah 49:1) = as to the truths of this good; (whereas) "from the womb" = as to the good of love.

@750[7]. "Bowels" (Ezekiel 7:19) = the will of good; and they are said "not to be filled" when there is no good in the Church.

@837[2]. The uses, from which, in which, and for which, the members and viscera of the body have been formed.

Visible. See <See-Conspicere>.

Visible.; Aspectabilis.

@HH 1. (The idea that) the whole visible world will perish. @LJ 1[2].

@TCR 768. Not to destroy the visible heaven. General article.

Visible.; Visibilis.

@AC 1519. The spheres of the Angels are sometimes presented visible...

@1869. The ideas themselves appear visible...

@4075[3]. Unless they... present the hidden God visible to themselves...

@5278[end]. Thoughts are sometimes there presented visible...

@8458[2]. When truths and goods are presented visible...

@10159. Almost all in the universe worship God under a visible form... This is implanted. Explained.

@10194[end]. In this way the Spiritual World presents itself visible there.

@HH 79[end]. See <Invisible>.

@514[end]. All these... cherish the idea that God is... visible under the human form.

@EU 7. In other Earths all who are not idolaters acknowledge the Lord as the Only God; for they adore the Divine not as an invisible, but as a visible Divine. Explained. @158[3].

@LJCont 23. All the visible things of the Spiritual World are correspondences of the affections of the Spirits and Angels.

@DLW 201. (Of this) little can be Known from the visible things in the natural world; but clearly from the visible things in the Spiritual World.

@222. (This) cannot be illustrated by examples from visible things, because the least things are not visible -exstant- to the eyes...

@228. These things may seem paradoxical, because they are not shown by applications to visible things; yet abstract things... are usually better comprehended than applied ones...

@349. That the visible things in the created universe testify that... @CL 417. @TCR 12[5].

@AR 11[2]. (The Tartars) said that they worship Jehovah, some as an invisible, and some as a visible, God.

@CL 416[2]. In invisible, as in visible, things; that is, in animalculae as in... great beasts.

@TCR 159[2]. Maintaining that... the Son is not to be worshipped, because He is... visible.

@--[7]. God is the Life and Salvation of all who believe in Him as visible...

@188[6]. For, by the Human of the Lord, Jehovah God... has made Himself visible before the eyes of men, and thus accessible; in like manner as He made Himself visible... to the Ancients, but then through an Angel.

@296[2]. In the second and third stories (of the mental house) are they who acknowledge and believe in one God under a visible human form...

@339. We ought to believe... in God the Saviour Jesus Christ, because this is to believe in a visible God in whom is the invisible; and faith in a visible God, who is at the same time both Man and God, enters into man. (Explained.)

@538. Therefore He came into the world, and made Himself visible, accessible, and conjoinable. @786[end], Illustrated.

@647[2]. Whereas the faith of the New Church is in a visible, accessible, and conjoinable God, in whom - as the soul is in the body - is the invisible, inaccessible, and unconjoinable God.

@787. The reason this New Church is the crown of all the Churches... is that it will worship one visible God, in whom is the invisible God, as the soul is in the body. The reason why the conjunction of God with man is possible in this and in no other way, is that man is natural. Explained.

@--. Conjunction with a visible God illustrated by comparisons.

@--. For all conjunction of God with man must be reciprocal, (which is impossible) except with a visible God.

@--[2]. That God was not visible before the assumption of the Human. Illustrated.

@--. That there is conjunction with the invisible God through Himself visible, thus through the Lord. Illustrated.

@SE 3869. They made their ideas visible near me. (Explained.)

@5742. They did not want to know anything about a visible God, but about an invisible one. They were told that the Lord also is an invisible God; for He is one with the Father, and in the Sun, and He is invisible in this world ever since His ascension from the sepulchre... but they were all unwilling [to hear] this...

Vision.; Visio.
Visionary.; Visionarius.

@AC 125. The men of the Most Ancient Church... were instructed by means of (most delicious and paradisiacal) visions and dreams. @597, Explained. (And there was insinuated into them what they signified. @1122.) @2179[3].

@1532. The visions of the prophets were... openings of their interior sight. Enumerated. @1619. @1626.

@1584. The external man... is then illuminated by the internal, and is then in the Divine vision here treated of... The Lord, when a boy, was, as to His external man, very often in such Divine sight...

@1784. "Vision" (Genesis 15:1) = inmost revelation, which is that of perception. (For) visions are according to the man's state. A vision presented before those whose interiors have been closed, is very differently circumstanced from a vision which is presented before those whose interiors are open. Example(s).

@--. There are many kinds of visions... The more interior the visions are, the more perfect they are. With the Lord they were the most perfect of all, because He had, at the time, a perception of all things in the World of Spirits and in the Heavens; and He had an immediate communication with Jehovah. This communication is represented... by "the vision" in which Jehovah appeared to Abraham.

@1882-1885. Two extraordinary kinds of vision, called "being withdrawn from the body," and "being carried by the spirit to another place." Described. @HH 440. @441.

@1885. But the things ordinarily seen (by Swedenborg) were not visions; but were things seen in the highest wakefulness of the body.

@1966. On visions and dreams, including the prophetical ones of the Word. General article.

@1967. Visions which are seen in phantasy, and which are illusions. Explained. @SE 1752.

@--[end]. These persons are visionaries.

@1968. Enthusiastic Spirits... have visions about things to be believed. Explained.

@1970. By genuine visions are meant the visions or sights of the Things which really exist in the other life... and which appear to a man when his interior sight is opened by the Lord... Such were the visions of the prophets. Described.

@1971. The visions which take place before good Spirits, are representatives of the Things which are in Heaven. Explained... Such things are perpetual with good Spirits.

@1972. The visions, or rather sights, which appear before the eyes of the spirit... are more and more interior. Described.

@1973. The kinds of vision are too numerous to mention.

@--. Two visions described by way of illustration. @1974. See also @1977.

@1975. (Representative) dreams inflow from Heaven: equally with visions, but with the difference that dreams do so when the body is asleep, and visions when it is not asleep.

@2162[4]. A vision of Daniel Explained. @AE 316[16]. @594[3].

@3301[2]. "A vision" = truths; here (Zechariah 13:4) falsities.

@4715[3]. "The valley of vision" (Isaiah 22:1) = phantasies from sensuous things about spiritual things.

@6000. God said to Israel in the visions of the night (Genesis 46:2) = an obscure revelation... For revelations took place either by dreams, by visions of the night, by visions of the day, or (in other ways).

@6836. "I will turn aside and see this great vision" (Exodus 3:3) = reflection upon this revelation... "A vision" = revelation. It is called "a great vision," because, in the supreme sense, by "the flame in the bush" is signified the Divine truth united to the Divine good in the Lord's Human.

@9248. "A vision of vanity" (Ezekiel 12:24) = a false revelation.

@--[2]. By to "see," or by "a vision," when predicated of the prophets, is signified a revelation which regards doctrine; and by to "divine" is signified a revelation which regards life.

@10042. The prophetic visions of the Word. Explained.

@10833[end]. (In the Sixth Earth) a Divine vision is distinguished from a vision which is not Divine (by the appearing of an Angel); for in a vision not Divine no Angel appears.

@HH 249[2]. Such are visionaries and enthusiasts. Described.

@456[3]. As they wondered that this has not been manifested to man by means of visions... they were told from Heaven that it could have been done... but still (such) would not have believed; and besides that it is dangerous to confirm anything by visions with those who are in falsities, because they would first believe, and afterwards deny, and would thus profane the truth... @TCR 282, Explained.

@LJCont 35. I asseverate that these things are not visions; but sights in complete wakefulness.

@90. The sensation (which the Moravians feel) is from visionary Spirits.

@DLord 52. We read of the prophets that they were "in vision"; and also that "Jehovah spoke to them." When they were in vision, they were not in their bodies, but in their spirit, in which state they saw such things as there are in Heaven... In their state of vision the eyes of their spirits were opened, and the eyes of their bodies were closed; and they then also seemed to themselves to be carried from place to place, the body remaining in its own place. In this state were, sometimes, Ezekiel, Zechariah, Daniel, and John when he wrote the Apocalypse; and it is said, then, that they were "in vision," or "in the spirit." Illustrated. @AR 36. @945[2].

@DP 134. That no one is reformed by means of visions... because they compel. Explained.

@--. Visions are of two kinds: Divine, and diabolical. Divine visions are effected by means of the representatives in Heaven; but diabolical visions by means of the magical things which are in Hell. There are also fantastic visions, which are the deceptive mockeries of an abstracted mind. Divine visions are such as were those of the prophets, who, when in them, were not in the body, but in the spirit; for visions cannot appeal to any man in wakefulness of the body; and therefore when they appeared to the prophets it is said that they were "in the spirit" Illustrated.

@--[4]. Such were the visions which appeared from Heaven before the sight of their spirits, and not before that of their bodies. Such visions do not happen at this day, for if they did they would not be understood, because they are effected by means of representatives...

@--. Diabolical visions, however, have sometimes happened, being induced by enthusiastic and visionary Spirits, who, from the delirium in which they were, called themselves the Holy Spirit. But these Spirits have now been collected together by the Lord, and cast into a Hell separate from the Hells of others.

@AR 7. The things which John saw were only visions... These see in John's visions arcana...

@36. The spiritual state in which John was when in the visions. Signified.

@--[end]. But the Word was not revealed in a state of the spirit, that is, in vision...

@229[end]. The things which John saw were visions which were representative...

@449. "I saw the horses in the vision" (Revelation 9:17) = that... the reasonings... were imaginary and visionary. Explained. ( = the falsification of the understanding of the Word. @AE 575.)

@451. "Their heads" = imaginary and visionary things about faith alone, which are called phantasies.

@--[2]. What are faith in act, and faith in state... but visionary things?... What is the remission of sins and the consequent instantaneous Salvation but a thing of visionary thought? (Other examples of these visionary things of faith alone.)

@CL 233[end]. All such are in posterior vision, and not in any prior sight.

@268. The visionary concupiscence, or phantasy, of possessing all wealth. Described.

@TCR 157. By being "in the spirit"... is meant a state of the mind in which it is separate from the body; and as, in this state, the prophets saw such things as come forth in the Spiritual World, it is called "the vision of God." Explained and ill. This is the state in which I have been for twenty-six years, with this difference: that I have been in the spirit and at the same time in the body...

@345[7]. A visionary and absurd faith... is falsity appearing like truth from ingenious confirmation.

@SE 651. (Of the four kinds of spiritual sight) the second, is vision with the eyes closed. Described. @2951.

@1752. On visions which are illusions. General article. @1755.

@1756. Unless a man is in faith in the Lord, he may easily be led to believe that such (illusory) visions are from Heaven, when yet they are of the devil; for they cannot be distinguished from true visions... except by those who are led by the Lord. But at this day such things are forbidden...

@1934. I saw direful visions... but still even in this injected terror, I felt secure.

@2244. (A Spirit who could produce visions which gave delight; but he afterwards inflicted injury.)

@2445. A vision concerning the interiors of the Word. Described.

@2498. (This) was shown me by a vision. Described.

@3015. A representative vision about the Quakers. Described.

@3135. A vision about the more subtle magicians. Described.

@3611. Such were represented in a semi-waking nocturnal vision. Described.

@4128. (This) was not speech, but vision, accompanied with a manifest perception of the Thing.

@4575. On a vision of a house and the Spirits there, and also of a city and buildings. Described.

@4663. I was in a waking vision. Described. @4773. @4784.

@4772. Where there is enlightenment, there must also be a vision of the contraries.

@5144. I was in a nocturnal vision, or dream. Described.

@5806. This has been shown me in a vision of the night. Described.

@5896. They said to him that these things were visions, and not real. He replied that he knew they were visions, but as he saw them with his eyes, and felt the pain... it must be real.

@DMin 4647. (This) is perceived by interior vision.

@4693. The man supposes that (this) is an illusion, or vision. Described.

@AE 177[7]. That they have completely deprived themselves of truths, and immersed themselves in falsities, is described by, "They said to the seers. See not; and to those that have vision, See not for us right things, speak unto us smooth things; see illusions" (Isaiah 30:10).

@236[6]. The Intellectual of those of the Church... is enlightened when the Word is read; and therefore it is said... "I will multiply vision" (Hosea 12:10). "Vision" = the truths of doctrine.

@237[3]. "A vision from the prophet" (Ezekiel 7:26) = doctrine; here, doctrine of what is false. ( = the understanding of the Word. @624[17].)

@369[end]. John was with these (lowest Angels) when in the spirit, that is, in vision.

@372[2]. That (these) will see evils, and divine falsities, is signified by, "It shall be night unto you for vision, and darkness... for divination" (Micah 3:6).

@375[18]. To "seal up vision and the prophet" (Daniel 9:24) = to close up and fulfil the things said in the Word about the Lord. ( = the end of the external (representative) Church, and the beginning of an internal, spiritual, Church. "Vision and the prophet" = the falsities of doctrine. = also that the Lord will fulfil all things foretold of Him in the Word. @624[20].)

@411[17]. By "the valley of vision" is signified falsity of doctrine confirmed by the sense of the letter...

@462[end]. This was a prophetic vision, which is such that the things seen are significative. @471.

@575. To "see in vision" (as distinguished from "in the spirit") = what is from fallacies.

@--[2]. The visions which, and from which, a man or the spirit of a man sees, are of two kinds - real, and not real. Real visions are visions of such things as really appear in the Spiritual World, which correspond exactly to the thoughts and affections of the Angels... Such were the visions with the prophets who prophesied truths; and such were the visions which appeared to John... The visions which are not real appear in the external form like real visions, but not in the internal form: they are produced by Spirits by means of phantasies: such were the visions with the prophets who prophesied vain things, or lies. All these latter visions, because not real, are fallacies, and therefore they - fallacies. (These two kinds of visions fully explained. @--[3].)

@624[8]. To "see visions" (Joel 2:28) = to perceive revelation.

@--[14]. "Night unto you for vision" (Micah 3:6) = the understanding of what is false instead of that of what is true.

@684[21]. "Thou hast spoken in vision to thy Holy One" (Psalms 89:19) = a prophetic arcanum concerning the Lord.

@701[32]. To "make a vision with Hell" (Isaiah 28:15) = divination, as if prophetic, from Hell.

@1037. Into a place appearing in vision which corresponded to the state of that religiosity. Signified, Explained.

@--. "In the spirit" = in vision; for what John saw in the spirit, he saw in vision. To see in vision is to see such things as come forth with the Angels in Heaven, which are representative... of spiritual things. Explained.

@1051. An amazing vision, in which there were arcana of Heaven that were unknown to him. Signified, Explained.

@1155[4]. If man could be reformed by means of miracles and visions, all in the world would be reformed... This way (of man's regeneration in freedom) is closed by miracles and visions. @--[5]. Explained.

@1156[2]. What those who want miracles and visions are like. Illustrated.

Visit.; Visitare.
Visitation.; Visitatio.

@AC 1850. "I will Judge" = visitation and Judgment.

@1857[4]. Visitation does not come until the evil (of the Church) has been consummated; that is, when there is no longer any good of charity and truth of faith. @2141.

@2242. "I will go down, and see" = visitation.

@--. The last time of the Church in general, and that of each person in particular, is called in the Word "visitation," and precedes the Judgment: thus "visitation" is nothing else than an examination of quality.

@--[4]. By "visitation," as mentioned in the Word, is signified either vastation... or deliverance; thus the examination of the quality. Illustrated.

@2318. "There came two Angels to Sodom in the evening" = the visitation which precedes the Judgment.

@--. In this chapter (Genesis 19) there is described the act of visitation itself, and then the Judgment.

@2323. "Evening" = the time of visitation. Explained, Illustrated.

@2345. The first time of the visitation. Signified, Explained.

@2616. "Jehovah visited Sarah" (Genesis 21:1) = the presence of the Divine Celestial in the Divine Spiritual... To "visit" = to be present.

@2906[3]. The same time is called "the year of visitation." Illustrated. (And "the day of visitation." @5360[2].)

@6588. "God in visiting will visit you" (Genesis 1:24) = that the last time will come... that is, the last time of the old Church, and the first of the new. This last time is called in the Word "visitation," which is predicated... both of the new Church which is being born, and of the old Church which is expiring; and, in particular, both of a man of the Church who is being saved, and of one who is being condemned. Illustrated. @6591.

@--[4]. To "visit" = to deliver.

@--[5]. "The day of visitation" (Luke 19:44) = the advent of the Lord, and enlightenment then; but, relatively to the Jewish nation... the last time of the representatives of the Church with them.

@--[end]. "Visitation" = retribution, thus condemnation. Illustrated.

@6895. "Visiting I have visited you" (Exodus 3:16) = His advent to those of the Spiritual Church; for to "visit" = the advent of the Lord, which precedes the last time of the Church, which time, in the Word, is called "the Last Judgment." Illustrated.

@--[end]. Thus "in visiting to visit" = deliverance from falsities, and thus initiation into the things of the Lord's Church and Kingdom.

@7066. "Jehovah hath visited the sons of Israel" (Exodus 4:31) = that those of the Spiritual Church were delivered and saved by the advent of the Lord; for to "visit" = deliverance by means of the advent of the Lord into the world; thus also Salvation.

@7273. Their condemnation (there) does not take place until they have been visited, that is, examined.

@7284. The state and quality of the Law from the Divine, with those of the Spiritual Church, at the first time of visitation. Signified.

@8876. To "visit the iniquity of the fathers" (Exodus 20:5) = the prolification of evils.

@10509. "In the day of My visitation, I will visit upon them their sin" (Exodus 32:34) = their last state in particular and in general when is the Judgment; for "the day of visitation" = the last state of the Church in particular and in general; and to "visit sin" = to be judged and condemned. It is said in particular and in genera], because the day of visitation happens to everyone... when he comes into the other life... and also to the Church in general, when it ceases to be...

@10622. At the consummation (of the Church) its visitation takes place; and when visitation is effected, all who are in evil are rejected, and all who are in good are received. Visitation takes place in the other life, where all are together...

@10623. "Visiting the iniquity of the fathers..." (Exodus 34:7) = the rejection and condemnation of evils...

@--[3]. The reason "visitation" = casting out and damnation, is that this follows the consummation of evils, and precedes the condemnation itself which is meant by "the Last Judgment "; for "visitation" is the examination of the quality of the man; but it takes place in the other life...

@10810[end]. (A visitation in the World of Spirits.) Described.

@LJ 54[2]. The "writing on the wall," and the death of Belshazzar = visitation and destruction...

@61. After visitation, destruction took place; for visitation always precedes. Visitation is the examination of their quality, and is also the separation of the good from the evil, the good being taken away, and the evil left.

@LJCont 23. On the signs and visitations before the Last Judgment. General article.

@26. Visitations were made by Angels; for visitation always precedes the perishing of any badly ordered Society. The Angels exhorted them to desist... and examined them to see whether any good [Spirits] were intermingled among them: these they separated. The crowd attacked the Angels, just as at Sodom.

@SE 4930. See <Last Judgment>. @5056. @5077. @5185. @5254. @5272. @5273. @5274. @5276. @5341. @5396. @5419. @5650. @5651. @5858.

@5667. Preachers visit the maidens there, and examine them.

@AE 144. That if not, when visitation comes, they will be dispersed. Signified.

@--[end]. To "come quickly" = visitation, because the advent of the Lord into the world = visitation. Visitation is the examination of man after death to [determine] his quality, before he is judged.

@173. Steadfastness in a state of the good of love and of faith, even to visitation. Signified.

@--[end]. "Till I come" = visitation.

@391[29]. It is said to "visit" (Amos 3:14) instead of to "judge," because visitation always precedes Judgment.

@401[20]. To "visit" (Isaiah 24:21) = to destroy, because visitation precedes Judgment...

@419[12]. The visitation which precedes the Last Judgment. Signified.

@624[12]. "The days of visitation," and "of retribution" (Hosea 9:7) = the days of the Last Judgment, when the evil suffer penalties, which is the "retribution" that is always preceded by "visitation."

@627. The mode of visitation, that is, of the exploration of the quality of the Church as to truth and as to good. Signified, Explained.

@--. The reason "a reed" = visitation, is that visitation is the exploration of the quality of the men of the Church; and because visitation precedes the Last Judgment. The nature of this visitation or exploration is evident from the visitation in Sodom. Explained.

@--[2]. "A reed" = Divine truth in the ultimate of order... by (which) and its power all visitation, or exploration, is effected. Explained.

@654[48]. The visitation of the natural man from Divine truth spiritual natural. Signified. For visitation is examination into what a man is, and the examination is effected by means of Divine truth.

@910. Announcement after exploration or visitation. Signified, Explained. @917.

@--. Visitation is mentioned in many passages, and it = an exploration of what the state of the Church is before the judgment. Not that such visitation actually occurs. Explained.

Vita vella.; Vita vella.

@SE 6063. @6090. @LJPost 332.

Vital.; Vitalis.
See <Heat>, and <Life>.

@AC 179. As soon as the interior bodily things grow cold, the vital substances are separated from the man. Described. So that nothing vital can remain.

@1860. They who are in hatred, perceive... a something vital in it.

@10201[2]. The good of love is the vital fire itself.

@HH 446. All the vital motions depend on this.

@DLW 379. Love is the origin of the vital heat. @CL 380[12]. @ISB 6[2].

@AR 320. "Pale" = what is not vital; (and this), in the Word, exists with those who are not in goods of life from truths of doctrine.

@AE 992[2]. For the Vital of the husband adds itself to the Vital of the wife...

Vituperate.; Vituperare.
Vituperation. Censure.; Vituperatio. Vituperium.

@AC 5567. He was against all whom he could dexterously... refute and vituperate. @SE 3485.

@5721[3]. They use many arts to infuse weariness and consequent weakness, especially vituperations and defamations.

@6203[end]. He then makes [evils] allowable... such as... vituperations...

@8318[2]. (Those in the love of self) not only despise others... but also pursue them with censures ... @9348[7].

@HH 462. a. [5]. There was one who accounted it as nothing to vituperate others: I heard his vituperations enumerated in order...

@CL 297. If women were to court (men) they would not only be censured...

@TCR 405[3]. If they honour Divine things, it is only lest they be... censured.

@SE 4789. He vituperated him from whom he could not gain anything.

@DMin 4706. They do not appear proud in the external form... for, when vituperated... they cared nothing...

@AE 654[55]. The vituperation of doctrine from the natural man. Signified.

@778[12]. Under <Blaspheme>, see this reference.

Vitus.; Vitus.

@TCR 367[end]. Like St. Vitus's dance, or the dance of St. Guy, which is caused by the bite of the tarantula.

@SE 3895. They rotated themselves horizontally, as usually in the dance of St. Vitus, which signified...

Viva voce. See <Swedenborg>.

@AC 9416. (The ten commandments) were uttered _viva voce_ by the Lord...

@9905. An answer was given (by the Urim and Thummim) _viva voce_.

@10355[4]. Angels from Heaven spoke _viva voce_ with some of (the Israelites).

@AR 36[end]. The Word was not revealed in... vision; but was dictated by the Lord to the prophets _viva voce_.

@SE 457. From a living voice I know that...

Vivacity.; Vivacitas. @CL 359[end].

Vivid.; Vividus. @AC 1622.

Vivify.; Vivificare.
Vivification.; Vivificatio.

@AC 156. "Bone" = the proprium not much vivified: "flesh" = the proprium vivified.

@671[end]. Truth and good vivified by the Lord. Described.

@726. To "make seed alive" (Genesis 7:3) = the truths of faith. Explained.

@--. Those are said to be "made alive" who receive the Lord's life. Explained.

@731. The proprium of man, when vivified, is as if blotted out. Signified.

@1474. "They will kill me, and will make thee live" (Genesis 12:12) = that they would not care for celestial things, but only for mere Knowledges.

@1589[2]. Celestial love vivifies everything into which it inflows; it even vivifies affections of evil.

@1771[end]. What the Word is when the Lord vivifies it... and when He does not vivify it.

@1776[end]. The Word is vivified in the reader by the Lord...

@1909. How the end is vivified by the life.

@2955. To "bury" = to be vivified, because they are in the course of receiving faith. Explained.

@5114[2]. The light of Heaven... then vivifies the things which are of the light of the world...

@5680[end]. The things in the Natural are vivified by influx from the Spiritual World.

@5890. "God sent me before you to make alive -ad vivificationem-" (Genesis 45:5) = spiritual life in them by Providence. @5898.

@--. That "vivification," and to "vivify," = spiritual life, that is, new life through regeneration. Explained, Illustrated.

@6008. That the Celestial Internal will vivify. Signified, Explained.

@6013. The interior things which vivify truth...

@6161. "Thou hast made us live" (Genesis 47:25) = spiritual life no otherwise...

@--. In what precedes, it has treated of the vivification, or regeneration, of the Natural, the whole process being described.

@6230. Prediction concerning vivification. Signified, Explained.

@--. Not that the descendants of Jacob were vivified; but those who are in the truth of faith and good of charity.

@6231. Vivification by means of the good of charity and the truth of faith. Signified, Explained.

@6574. To "make to live a great people" (Genesis 1:20) = that hence is life for those who are in the truths of good. To "make to live" = spiritual life. References.

@6680. "They kept the boys alive" (Exodus 1:17) = that truths, being of good, were preserved. To "keep alive" = to preserve.

@8409[3]. "It is the spirit that quickeneth" (John 6:63).

@--. All who are being regenerated, are vivified from what is proper to the Lord. Signified.

@8456. As (the Divine truth which proceeds from the Lord) is the inmost, it... vivifies the truth which is beneath. Treated of.

@8891. The regeneration and vivification of those things which are in the internal and external man. Signified, Explained.

@9189. "Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live" (Exodus 22:18) = [no] deprivation of spiritual life; (for) those deprive themselves of spiritual life who conjoin with the truths of faith falsities from the evil of the love of self. @9188[2].

@9295[2]. "Waving" = vivification; for truths are not alive with a man until they are in good.

@10262. For (the Lord's Divine celestial good) vivifies all things through the Divine truth which proceeds from it; and it vivifies them according to the quality of the reception.

@DSS 19. The Word vivifies those who read it holily.

@DFaith 32. This spiritual heat... vivifies the knowledges of truth and good...

@DLW 93. The spiritual Sun by its heat vivifies spiritual beings... loo, God... through this Proceeding, vivifies and enlightens Angels and men... Therefore, vivification and enlightenment are said to be effected through the Spirit of Jehovah.

@AR 200. The Word, from this life, vivifies the affections of the will of the man who reads it holily. Signified.

@475. He who vivifies all in Heaven and the Church, and each and all things with them. Signified, Explained.

@510. That these two essentials of the New Church ... are vivified by the Lord with those who receive them. Signified, Explained.

@CL 256. Plays, music, etc., are sweetnesses, because they are vivifications.

@TCR 40. The life which is the light that proceeds from the spiritual Sun... as it illumines, so it also vivifies, the understanding of man.

@142. That the Divine virtue and operation meant by "the Holy Spirit," are, in general, reformation and regeneration; and, according to these... vivification, etc. General article. @149.

@--[2]. Through Divine truth from Good, that is, through faith from charity, man is... vivified, etc.

@364. Thus God, from His life, vivifies every man; and that, without this vivification, man would be, in flesh a mere sponge, and in bones a mere skeleton...

@--[2]. The Divine love as heat, and the Divine wisdom as light, inflow into human minds... and vivify them according to the quality of the form...

@385[2]. This quickening (of vegetation in the spring) may be seen to the life in the Spiritual World.

@618[end]. By the conjunction of (spiritual light and heat) the Lord vivifies and regenerates man.

@SE 158[end]. Consent... vivifies my mind.

@5011. Those who are "Babel"... laboured to vivify (Charles XII).

@AE 186[2]. To "make alive the souls that should not live" (Ezekiel 13:19) = to persuade them that eternal life is from falsities.

@386[18]. To "keep them alive in famine" (Psalms 33:19) = to give spiritual life according to the desire.

Vocabulary.; Vocabularium.

@SE 2263. That the philosophy of men is only a vocabulary. Explained.

Voetius.; Voetius.
Voetians.; Voetiani.

@SE 6099. On Cocceius and Voetius. General article.

@--[8]. On the Voetians. @--[10]. @--[11]. @--[13].

Voice.; Vox.
See also <Word-Vox>.

@AC 219. "The voice of Jehovah God..." (Genesis 3:8) = a dictate... (for) in the Word," the voice of Jehovah" stands for the Word itself, the doctrine of faith, conscience or internal advertence, and also the consequent reproof; and therefore even thunderbolts are called "voices of Jehovah." Illustrated.

@--[2]. "A voice" = revelation. Illustrated.

@220. "The voice of one crying" (Isaiah 40:3) = the annunciation of the Lord's advent; in general, for every (such) annunciation, as with the regenerate, who have a dictate.

@374. "The voice of thy brother's bloods" (Genesis 4:10) = violence inflicted on charity. In the Word, "voice" stands for everything that accuses.

@375. "A voice crying," and "the voice of a cry," is a wonted formula of the Word, and is applied to any case in which a noise, tumult, or disturbance, and also in which anything happy, occurs. Illustrated.

@448. I have spoken with many (Spirits) in as clear a voice, although internal, as with friends here.

@1395. There is an image of the deceit in every tone of the voice.

@2240[6]. "The voice of weeping shall be no more heard in her, nor the voice of crying" (Isaiah 65:19) = chat there shall not be evil, nor falsity. @2351.

@2689. "She lifted up her voice and wept" (Genesis 21:16) = a further degree of grief. For to "lift up the voice and weep" = the last degree of grief, because weeping with an uplifted voice is nothing else.

@2691. "God heard the voice of the boy" (verse 17) = aid then. Explained.

@3563. "The voice is the voice of Jacob" (Genesis 27:22) = that in this case the Intellectual of truth was within... thus in inverted order. For "voice" is predicated of truth.

@3849. Voice (or a word) without affection, is like the voice of an automaton, thus is only sound without life; but in proportion to the degree and the quality of affection there is in it, in the same proportion is the degree and the quality of the life in it.

@3893. For Spirits and Angels have, among themselves, a sonorous voice; and are heard by one another as well as a man is heard by a man; but human singing is not to be compared, in sweetness and harmony, with theirs.

@4060[8]. "He shall send forth His Angels with... a great voice" (Matthew 24:31) = election; not that this is done by... great voices, but by the influx of... holy truth... "A trumpet and a great voice" = evangelization.

@4311[3]. It matters not from whom the voice of good and truth proceeds...

@5121[2]. But those who are not in good and truth can have no revelation from perception, but by a living voice heard in them... This revelation is external.

@5313[6]. "The voices," etc. which proceeded out of the throne (Revelation 4) = the terrors caused by the Divine truth with those who are not in good.

@5933. "The voice was heard in Pharaoh's house" (Genesis 45:16) = that this infilled the universal Natural; for "a voice" which is heard elsewhere, and at a distance, when predicated of influx. = to infill; for as a voice which is heard infills, so does that which inflows.

@6616. When I heard Spirits speaking to me, I could perceive, merely from the tone of voice of the speech, whether they spoke from what was simulated, etc.

@6832[6]. "The voice of Jehovah" (Psalms 29:7) = the Divine truth.

@6971. "If they do not hear the voice of the former sign" (Exodus 4:8) = if they do not obey what is announced from the Word... "A voice" = what is announced from the Word. @--[3], Illustrated.

@--[3]. "A voice" is often predicated of... things which do not belong to a voice. Illustrated.

@--[4]. "A voice" = annunciation; and, in a good sense, annunciation from the Word, which voice is called "the voice of Jehovah." Illustrated.

@--[end]. "A voice" = Divine truth, thus the Word, and annunciation from it. Illustrated.

@6985. That voice and speech from the Divine are neither heard nor perceived. Signified, Explained.

@--. "Mouth" = voice... because it is the organ of the voice (whereas the tongue is the organ of speech). The difference between voice and speech is evident to everyone; and also that to be heard is predicated of voice, and to be perceived, of speech.

@6996[2]. The last mediation (by which the Divine truth passes to man) is by a Spirit with the man, who inflows either into his thought, or by a living voice.

@7095. "Who is Jehovah that I should hear His voice" (Exodus 5:2) = contrary thought about the Lord in respect to hearkening to His exhortation; for "voice," here, = exhortation... thus to "hear the voice" = to obey or hearken to the exhortation.

@7573. "Jehovah gave voices" (Exodus 9:23) = the recession and separation of the communication with those who are in good and truth; for "the voices," which were those of thunders, = the Divine truths which enlighten and perfect those who are in Heaven, and terrify and devastate those who are in Hell; and, as they devastate these, they (have the above signification). @7592. @7597.

@--[2]. That the "voices," which are those of thunders = the truths Divine which enlighten and perfect those who are in Heaven, and terrify and devastate those who are in Hell. Illustrated.

@8313[3]. "Their voice resounds like the sea" (Jeremiah 6:23) = the derivative reasoning.

@8360. "If... thou wilt hear the voice of Jehovah thy God" (Exodus 15:26) = faith in the precepts of the Lord... "The voice of Jehovah" = what is enunciated from the Word, thus the precept of the Lord.

@8764[4]. "Its voice as the voice of wheels, and as the voice of Shaddai" (Ezekiel 1:24, etc.) = (the quality of Divine truth in Heaven); for... "voice" is attributed to Divine truth; and it is therefore said "the voice of great waters," because "waters" = truths; and "the voice of the wheels," because "wheels" = the truths of doctrinal things; and also "the voice of God Shaddai," because "God Shaddai" = truth chiding in temptation and afterwards consoling. References.

@8766. "If... ye will hear My voice" (Exodus 19:5) = the reception of truth; for... "the voice of Jehovah" = the Word, thus truth Divine. References.

@8813. "There were voices and lightnings" (verse 16) = a Divine state in which there was revelation; for "voices" which are the sounds of thunders, = truths Divine. Illustrated. @8914.

@8823. The voice of the trumpet (verse 19) = heavenly or angelic truth conjoined with Divine, thus what is general of revelation. Explained. @8915.

@8824. "God answered him in a voice" (Exodus 19:19) = the Divine truth _a quo_.

@9234[end]. The voice (of the Spirits of the moon) was emitted from the abdomen...

@9307. "Hear His voice" (Exodus 23:21) = obedience to the precepts which are from the Lord; for... "a voice," when predicated of the Lord, = truths Divine, thus the precepts which are from the Lord... and therefore also the Word and doctrine from it, are "the voice of Jehovah." References.

@9384. "All the people answered with one voice" (Exodus 24:3) = reception in the understanding by those who are truly of the Church; for... "voice" = the confession which comes forth from the understanding; for the things which belong to the mouth... correspond to the intellectual part...

@9406[6]. Truth Divine, or the Lord in ultimates, is meant (also) by "the voice of His words like the voice of a multitude" (Daniel 10:6).

@9741[5]. "The voice of the wings" (Ezekiel 10) = the truth of faith from good.

@9926. "His voice shall be heard" (Exodus 28:35) = the influx of truth with those in the Heavens and on earth; for... "a voice," when predicated of Aaron, by whom the Lord is represented, = Divine truth; for "a voice" = the annunciation of it, and... it is therefore with those in the Heavens and on earth; for the Divine truth infills all things of Heaven, and makes all things of the Church. Such an annunciation was represented by "the voice from the bells of gold "...

@--[2]. That "voice," in the Word, = the Divine truth which is heard and perceived in the Heavens and on earth. Illustrated.

@--[3]. "The voice of strangers" (John 10:5) = falsity.

@--[8]. The sound from the bells is (here) called "a voice"; and in other passages the sounds from trumpets, and also from thunders, are called "voices," and by these in like manner are signified Divine truths...

@10182[3]. "The voice of Jehovah" = the Divine truth which proceeds from His Divine good. Illustrated.

@10240[2]. Thou hearest the voice thereof (John 3:8) = that these things come to perception in the external or natural man; "voice" = what is annunciated from the Word. See @AE 419[6].

@10454. "Joshua heard the voice of the people in their shouting" (Exodus 32:17) = a survey and apperception as to what was the quality of the interiors of that nation... for by "voice," in the Word, is signified the interior voice, which is the thought, and thus the interior quality in respect to truth or falsity, for the thought comes from one of these...

@10455. "There is a voice of war in the camp" (Exodus 32:17) = an assault on truth and good... by falsities and evils... For "a voice" = thought and affection, which are the interior things of the voice, thus the quality of the interiors.

@10456. "It is not the voice of a shout-clamor is for victory, and it is not the voice of a shout for a Thing that is lost" (Exodus 32:18) = that Heaven acts on one side, and Hell on the other; thus falsity against truth, and truth against falsity; for "the voice of a shout"... = the quality of the interiors of that nation.

@10457. "The voice of a miserable shout do I hear" (Exodus 32:18) = the lamentable state of their interiors... for what is lamentable is expressed in the Original Language by "a voice," which = a shout, an affection, and misery; thus "a miserable shout"; and, as "a voice" = the quality of the interiors, "the voice of a miserable shout" = the lamentable state of the interiors.

@DSS 18[5]. "The voice of Jehovah," which, in this case (Psalms 29:3-9) is thunder, = Divine truth, or the Word, in its power.

@AR 37. "I heard behind me a great voice as of a trumpet" (Revelation 1:10) = a manifest perception of Divine truth revealed from Heaven. "A great voice," when heard from Heaven, = the Divine truth. Illustrated. (Why it was heard as a trumpet. Explained.) @AE 55.

@50. "His voice as the voice of many waters" (verse 15) = Divine truth natural. ( = Divine truth in ultimates. @AE 71.)

@--[2]. Thus the "voice of many waters" = the Lord's Divine truth in the Word. Illustrated.

@218. "If anyone shall hear My voice" (Revelation 3:20) = him who believes in the Word... To "hear the voice" = to believe in the Word; for the Divine truth of the Word is "the voice of Jehovah." ( = him who pays attention to the Lord's precepts... for "My voice" = the truths of the Word, of doctrine, and of the derivative faith, thus the precepts. @AE 249.)

@226. "The first voice which I heard was like that of a trumpet speaking to me" (Revelation 4:1) = the Divine influx... and the consequent manifest perception. ( = a revelation now of future things, clear and manifest. @AE 261, @AE 262.)

@--[2]. Voices like trumpets are heard in Heaven when convocations and disposings in order are taking place.

@236. "Voices (out of the throne)" (Revelation 4:5) = instruction from the Lord. Explained. ( = the perception of the Divine truth in the Heavens from the Lord. @AE 273.)

@258. "A mighty Angel proclaiming with a great voice" (Revelation 5:1) = Divine truth from the Lord inflowing deeply into the thought of Angels and men... "A great voice" = Divine truth from the Lord in power. ( = exploration by the influx of the Lord into Heaven. @AE 302.)

@258. "Saying with a great voice" (verse 12) = confession from the heart. ( = acknowledgement in the heart. @AE 337, Explained.)

@368. "Crying with a great voice" (Revelation 7:10) = acknowledgement from the heart. ( = adoration from the good of truth, and the consequent joy of heart. @AE 459.)

@396. "Voices" (Revelation 8:5) = reasonings about faith alone. Explained. @AE 498.

@416. "Saying with a great voice. Woe, woe, woe" (verse 13) = the deepest lamentation... "The rest of the voices of the trumpet of the three Angels..." = the exploration and manifestation of the state of the Church and of life... @AE 530. @531.

@437. "The voice of their wings" (Revelation 9:9) = reasonings. @AE 558.

@443. "I heard a voice" (verse 14) = a command from the Lord. ( = a revelation from the Lord. @AE 567.)

@471. "He cried with a great voice as when a lion roareth" (Revelation 10:3) = a grievous lamentation that the Church has been taken away from Him. ( = a testification of severe grief on account of the desolation of Divine truth in the Church. @AE 601.)

@472. Under <Thunder>, see this reference.

@520. "There were great voices in Heaven" (Revelation 11:15) = celebrations by the Angels, ( = enlightenment and joy in the higher Heavens. Explained. @AE 682.)

@553. "I heard a great voice saying in Heaven" (Revelation 12:10) = the joy of the Angels of Heaven. @AE 744.

@614. "I heard a voice from Heaven as the voice of many waters" (Revelation 14:2) = the Lord speaking through the New Heaven from Divine truths... For when a voice is heard from Heaven, it is from the Lord. Illustrated. ( = a Glorification of the Lord from the Divine truths which are from Him. Explained. @AE 854.) @AR 615. @616. @AE 855. @856.

@628. "Saying with a great voice, Fear God" (verse 7) an admonition that they should not do evils, because they are contrary to the Lord. ( = an exhortation. @AE 873.)

@639. "I heard a voice from Heaven saying unto me" (verse 13) = a prediction from the Lord. ( = consolation by the Lord after temptations. @AE 897.)

@645. "Crying with a great voice to Him that sat on the cloud" (verse 15) = a supplication of the Angels of Heaven to the Lord. ( = an annunciation after exploration! or visitation... For "a voice" involves the things that are said. @AE 910.)

@676. "I heard a great voice out of the temple" (Revelation 16:1) = an influx from the Lord from the inmost of Heaven. Explained. ( = a manifestation by Divine truth from the Word. @AE 959.)

@709. "There came a great voice out of the temple of Heaven from the throne" (verse 17) = a manifestation by the Lord from the inmost of Heaven. @AE 1013.

@710. "Voices, lightnings, and thunders" (verse 18) = reasonings, falsifications of truth, and argumentations, from the falsities of evil in the Church with those in faith alone... @AE 1014.

@760. "I heard another voice from Heaven" (Revelation 18:4) = an exhortation from the Lord to all, both those in that religiosity and those not in it. ( = an exhortation to those who are in truths and the good of life, to beware of such... "A voice from Heaven" being heard, means from the Lord through the Word; for all things which man imbibes from the Word are "a voice from Heaven." Further Explained. @AE 1106.)

@792. "The voice of harpers, etc. shall be heard in thee no more" (Revelation 18:22) = no spiritual affection... "Voice" means sound, and all sound corresponds to affection... ( = no longer any joys... @AE 1185.)

@794. (Nor) "the voice of a mill" (Revelation 18:22) = no searching for, investigation, or confirmation of, spiritual truth... ( = no understanding of truth from the will of good. @AE 1187.)

@797. (Nor) "the voice of the bridegroom and of the bride" (Revelation 18:23) = no conjunction of good and truth... "Voice," here, = joy, because it is that of the bridegroom and bride. ( = not any joy from the conjunction of good and truth. @AE 1189.)

@809. "A voice came out of the throne, saying, Praise our God..." (Revelation 19:5) = an influx from the Lord into Heaven, and thus the unanimity of the Angels that (these) should worship the Lord... @AE 1209.

@811. "I heard as it were the voice of a great multitude, and as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of mighty thunders, saying, Alleluia..." (verse 6) = the joy of the Angels of (the three Heavens)... "A voice" = the joy of the worship, confession, and celebration of the Lord. Explained. ( = a Glorification of the Lord by all in the Heavens, a Glorification of Him from truths, and a Glorification of Him from the goods of love... @AE 1214-1216.) @AR 803. @AE 1196.

@816[2]. When Angels speak to a man, they never speak to him from Heaven, but the voice which is heard thence is from the Lord through Heaven...

@831. "The Angel... cried with a great voice" (verse 17) = the Lord calling together (all such) from Divine zeal. For "a voice," or an influx from the Lord from the Divine Love, is from Divine zeal...

@882. "I heard a great voice out of Heaven saying" (Revelation 21:3) = the Lord, from love, speaking and evangelizing... By "a great voice" is meant speech from love; for "great" is predicated of love.

@CL 11. A voice was (then) heard from Heaven... @55[3].

@446. When the voice begins to become masculine.

@WE 7352. Voices heard coming from the hoofs of horses, from animals, etc. @SE 330. @1770.

@SE 3701. The voice (of the Sirens) was heard as if from a Society of the good. @4598.

@5672. Man cannot be enlightened by a living voice from Heaven. Explained.

@AE 261[2]. "Voice" = the proceeding Divine, which is the Divine truth. @--[3]. @644[19].

@262. A voice which is heard from Heaven with those who are in the spirit, is wont to be heard like a human voice; but this was heard like a trumpet speaking, because it was clearly perceived by the Angels...

@283[13]. "Voice" is predicated of truth. @304[50]. Illustrated @419[13].

@353. For the voices which descend from the Inmost Heaven into the hearing of a man, are heard (as thunder); for they fill the whole brain, and propagate themselves thence towards the hearing... It is different with the voices which descend from the Middle Heaven, which, being attended with enlightenment, are heard... like voices (or words) of speech. Explained.

@355[18]. "The voice of the horseman and the bowmen" (Jeremiah 4:29) = reasoning...

@422[end]. "Voice" = influx.

@424. "He cried with a great voice" (Revelation 7:2) = a Divine command. @AR 346.

@498. Such (reasonings, etc.) are heard in the Spiritual World as the voices of a murmuring, clashing, threatening, and fighting multitude; and, at a distance, where they are not heard, they appear as thunder and lightning... As these things originate from the flowing down of the Divine good and truth... the voices, thunders, and lightnings, when heard and seen by the good, = the Divine truth as to perception and enlightenment...

@604. I heard a voice from Heaven saying unto (Revelation 10:4) = a command from the Lord.

@614. "The voice which I heard from Heaven again spoke to me and said" (verse 8) = the exploration of the men of the Church as to the quality of their remaining understanding of the Word... for (this) voice from Heaven involves these things.

@650[57]. "A voice in the window" (Zephaniah 2:14) = the preaching of falsity.

@668. "They heard a great voice from Heaven saying to them"- (Revelation 11:12) = the Lord's Divine Providence... For by "a voice from Heaven" is signified all that proceeds from the Lord, which, in general, is called the Divine truth; and, with us in the world, the Word; thus, in special, every precept and commandment in the Word. This is called "a voice from Heaven" because it has descended from the Lord through Heaven... That it is the Lord's Divine Providence which is iere signified by "a voice from Heaven," is because it is treating of the state of Heaven and the Church at its end... @AR 512.

@702. "Voices" (verse 19) = reasonings. @AR 530.

@864[4]. To "know and hear the Lord's voice" (John 10:4, 27) = to do His commandments.

@884. "A great voice" (Revelation 14:9) = exhortation. @AR 633.

@899[8]. "They who hear the voice of the Son of God" (John 5:25) = those who live according to His commandments.

@1096. "A great voice" (Revelation 18:2) = joy of heart. Explained. @AR 755.

Void. See <Empty>.

Vallerius.; Vallerius. @SE 4858.

Volubility.; Volubilitas.
Volubly.; Volubiliter.

@AC 5388. (On some Spirits who can speak as volubly and quickly as heavenly Spirits, who yet are evil.) @SE 1168.

@8025. The volubility of the discourse (of the Spirits of Jupiter).

Volume. See <Roll-Volumen>.

Voluntary. See <Will>.

Voluptuous. See <Pleasure>.

Vomit. Vomiting.; Vomitus.
Vomiting.; Vomitio.
Vomiting out, A.; Evomitio.
Vomit out, To.; Evomere.
Vomitory.; Vomitalis.
See <Spew out>.

@AC 814. The stench from that Hell (of hatred, made me) vomit.

@1512. From those who have lived in hatred and revenge there exhale spheres which... excite vomiting.

@1513. One of those called "the Luke warm" came to me... and the Spirits then felt... as when men are moved to vomiting. @SE 793.

@1514. When the sphere of those who have contracted a nature from simulation is turned into an odour, there is a vomitory stench. @SE 1045.

@2269[3]. Evil would spew out good as something vomitory.

@5006[2]. At the mere thought of spiritual good and truth... they felt like what (here) excites vomiting.

@5702. @SE 4422[end].

@DLW 341[end]. When the Hells are slightly opened... they excite vomiting. @TCR 569[5].

@AR 204. "I will vomit thee out of My mouth" (Revelation 3:16) = to be separated from the Lord; and to be thus separated from Him, is to be in neither Heaven nor Hell, but in a place apart, bereaved of human life, where there are mere phantasies. The reason is that they have commingled truths with falsities, and goods with evils, thus holy things with profane, to such a degree that they cannot be separated... ( = separation from the Knowledges which are from the Word: not that the Lord separates them from Himself, but that they separate themselves from the Lord. To "vomit out" is mentioned, because it is treating of "the Luke warm," and what is Luke warm... causes vomiting out, which is from the correspondence. Explained. @AE 235.)

@--[2]. It is said of these that they are "vomited out," because the World of Spirits... corresponds to the stomach... and the things which are vomited out of the stomach are those which have not been separated (from what is excrementitious). It is on account of this correspondence that to be "vomited out," and "vomiting," are mentioned in the following passages. Illustrated. @TCR 132[end]. @683[end].

@SE 1278. (Infernal spheres by which) I was compelled to vomit out my food... the effect being vomiting -vomitio-.

@1842. Their state was represented by an infant... which vomited out milk. Explained.

@3587[end]. (The persuasive sphere of the Antediluvians causes vomiting in others.)

@4170. The reason lukewarm water causes vomiting. Explained.

@6100. On Dutchmen who pass their time in a vomitory stench... Some Societies of the Dutch, where are those whose wives have domineered over them... collected vessels full of vomit, and held their nostrils over them, being deliciated with this stench.

@AE 235[4]. Both these separations are meant by being "vomited out of the mouth." Fully illustrated.

@960[5]. Of falsified truth is predicated "shameful vomit" (Habakkuk 2:16).

@986[end]. Hence it is that from the brothels in the Hells there flow forth stenches which excite vomiting. @1005[end].

Vomiting. See <Spawning>.

Vortex.; Vortex.
Vortical.; Vorticalis.
Vorticillar.; Vorticillaris.

@DP 319[2]. (These changes and variations in the organic forms of the mind) can be expressed only in the words of spiritual language, the sound of which (here) would be vorticillar ingyrations and egyrations...

@TCR 79[2]. One of the philosophers said... Nature, in producing the universe... folded itself into vortexes, which dashed against each other...

@SE 279. The heavenly vortexes, or abodes, correspond to the parts of man. Explained.

@402[end]. The vortical fluxion of these Spirits proceeded easily.

@407. While these Spirits were flowing in vortical forms...

@4686. There appeared an encircling-circumiens form, which existed from the influx of Heaven, and a consequent operation into the Spirits and Genii around man; and this form was active, like a vortex... consisting of the influx of such Spirits or Societies from Hell...

@5057. In sinking down (the cities) appeared like a vortical gyration such as there is in volumes of water falling down through an opening... a sign that they cannot he saved. @LJPost 137.

@LJPost 320. The middle ether [is that] which makes a vortex around the planets, in which is light, and the satellites, and from which is magnetism.

Vote. See <Support-Suffragari>.

Votive.; Votivus.
See <Eucharist>.

@AC 3185. Devout wishes from Divine enlightenment. Signified.

@6091. A devout wish for conjunction. Signified. @6099.

@9323. A customary devout wish in the Ancient Churches, quoted.

@CL 16. They murmured a devout expression of praise to the Lord.

@24. The priest added a devout (or votive) prayer...

@54[4]. They obtain the wished-for liberty...

@261[end]. After a wish of peace.

@TCR 185[7]. After the priest had offered votive prayers at the altar...

@WE 6610. Gifts which were votive and spontaneous; the votive ones are not spontaneous...

Vow.; Votum.
Vow, To.; Vovere.

@AC 3732. "Jacob vowed a vow" (Genesis 38:20) = ... to will that the Lord may provide; and, in the supreme sense, a state of Providence. Explained. @4091.

@4091. "Where thou vowedst unto Me a vow" (Genesis 31:13) = what is holy. Explained.

@CL 155[2]. All monks and nuns are there freed from their vows... in order that they may be led to choose a life... according to the interior wishes and desires of their love.

@--[3]. Those who had vowed perpetual virginity...

@226. One may wish from the heart for a chaste marriage...

@297[end]. A duty of prayer.

@319. If there is a wish for more children.

@AE 433[11]. "Keep thy feasts, and perform thy vows" (Nahum 1:15) = to rejoice on account of His advent, and to worship Him then.

@684[26]. "He swore to Jehovah, and vowed to the Mighty One of Jacob" (Psalms 132:2) = an irrevocable asseveration before the Lord.

@725[11]. To "vow and sacrifice" (Malachi 1:14) = to worship...

Vowel.; Vocalis.*
Footnote: * The vowels named in this article are of course to be sounded as on the continent of Europe.
See <A (the letter, sounded as in father)>, <E (the letter, sounded like the a in Fate)>, <I (the letter, sounded as in pique)>, <O (the letter)>, and <U (the letter, sounded oo, as in rule)>.

@AC 793[2]. In (Hebrew words of the spiritual class) the first three vowels are usually dominant; in those of the celestial class, the last two vowels.

@HH 241. The speech of the celestial Angels has much of the sound of the vowels u, and o, and that of the spiritual Angels of the vowels e, and i; for the vowels are for sound; and in sound there is the affection...

@--. As the vowels do not pertain to language, but to the elevation of its words by means of sound to various affections according to the state of each person, the vowels have not been expressed in the Hebrew language, and they are variously pronounced. By this the Angels Know the quality of a man in respect to his affection and love.

@--[2]. The speech of the celestial Angels... rarely passes from consonant to consonant except by the interposition of a word which begins with a vowel; and hence it is that in the Word the particle "and" is so often interposed; (for) in the Hebrew this particle is soft, and sounds from a vowel both ways -utrinque-.

@261. In the angelic language... by the vowels they express affections.

@DSS 90[2]. In the Third Heaven... the vowels are for the sound, which corresponds to the affection; and in that Heaven they cannot utter the vowels i and e; but, instead of them, y and eu; and the vowels a, o, and u are in use among them, because they give a full sound. @DeVerbo 4[2].

@AR 29[2]. In the Spiritual World... a vowel, because it serves for sound, = something of affection or love. @TCR 19[2].

@SE 1645. That the celestial... prefer vowels. Explained.

@2631. Hence, (in the Hebrew) there have been no vowels, so that the sense of the letter was known from the interior sense... and therefore he who perceives the sense of the letter from the interior sense, understands better what is written in the Hebrew without vowels than with them.

@4866. Especially are the vowels of service (to Spirits), with much variety in the case of each person. Example(s).

@5112. When the spiritual Angels speak, their words... have an affinity with the vowels e, and i; and when they use a, there is still something of e or ae therein; and when they use u, there is something of i or y... Whereas the words of the celestial Angels have an affinity with a, o, and u, and therefore [their speech] falls into such words as contain these vowels. On this account, when a man is speaking to them, he is bent from words which contain e, and i, to those which contain a, o, and u.

@5620[end]. The celestial Angels said - as I too have often perceived - that they have not the vowels i and e; but a, o, and especially u; and that y is intermediate between what is celestial and what is spiritual; and as they... merely serve for sound, there are no vowels in the Hebrew language as in other languages; but they are added by means of marks above and below.

@5622. See <Hebrew language>.

@--[end]. In place of a (the celestials) use [a vowel] intermediate between a and o; in place of i they have what is almost y; and instead of ae they have eii.

@5787. The vowels are according to the nature of things - a, e, i, o, u - as is evident from the celestial Angels: u involves all things; and so on.

@5964[end]. (In Heaven) arcana are involved in a word by the vowels in respect to sound, and by the consonants in respect to the meaning.

@6063[2]. (In the Spiritual World) all the vowels = something that conjoins, as with, in, and so on. I, there, = that which is from what is interior; and so on.

@DWis 7. 5. (In Heaven) each vowel letter is an affection; and the vowel letters are not written, but pointed.

Vulcan.; Vulcanus. @TCR 137[12].

Vulture.; Vultur.

@TCR 123[4]. As if he felt a vulture in his bosom...

@381[end]. As to faith they appear like vultures.

@501[end]. Like vultures over cocks.

@Coro 40. A man who has no religion, is, in spiritual things, like a starving vulture devouring its own offspring.

